window.LUNA_CHAPTERS=(window.LUNA_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":76,"title":"Chapter 76 An Alpha’s Claim","paragraphs":["Alpha Sebastian grabbed Eira’s hand before she could move away.","\"What will it take for you to let this go? Name it. Money, a car, another house. Whatever you want.\"","His voice was gentle. His grip was not.","\"Remember what Miss Gwen told you about your name?\" he continued. \"Eira means snow in Welsh. She wanted you to stay kind through the worst winter and believe spring would come.\"","Years ago, Alpha Sebastian had called it a beautiful name. He had promised her a beautiful future.","Now he was using it to guilt her into protecting Isabella.","\"Tell the police you’re done cooperating,\" he said. \"You’re okay now. Let’s put this behind us.\"","\"I nearly drowned.\"","\"But you didn’t.\"","Eira stared at him.","Alpha Sebastian looked away. \"When we get home, you should apologize to Bella too.\"","For a second, Eira thought she had heard him wrong.","\"You want me to apologize to the woman who drugged me?\"","\"She didn’t mean for it to go that far.\"","\"She set me up to be assaulted.\"","\"She’s my sister.\"","\"And I’m your wife.\"","Alpha Sebastian’s jaw tightened.","\"My parents already had concerns about you. Now Bella’s been arrested because of your statement. If you keep pushing this, they’ll never accept you.\"","Eira let out a quiet, bitter laugh.","\"So you knew.\"","\"Knew what?\"","\"That they treated me like dirt. You knew, and you let it happen.\"","\"That’s not true. I stood up for you.\"","\"When?\"","\"I told them you were a good person. I tried to keep the peace.\"","\"You watched them tear me down for four years, and now you want credit for saying I’m nice?\"","\"I’m caught in the middle here!\" Alpha Sebastian snapped. \"Why can’t you meet me halfway?\"","\"There is no halfway between me and the people who tried to have me assaulted.\"","She ripped her hand free.","\"Let me out.\"","\"Eira, calm down.\"","\"Pull over.\"","The driver glanced at Alpha Sebastian in the rearview mirror.","\"Keep driving,\" Alpha Sebastian ordered.","Eira looked at him for one long second. Then she rolled down the window and threw her purse onto the shoulder.","Alpha Sebastian’s eyes widened. \"What the hell are you doing?\"","\"Getting out.\"","She started climbing through the window.","Alpha Sebastian lunged and caught her around the waist.","\"Eira!\"","Wind whipped through the car as he dragged her back inside.","\"Are you out of your damn mind? You could’ve died!\"","\"I told you to stop the car.\"","\"You’re threatening me with your own life?\"","---","In the car behind them, Alpha Killian saw Eira’s purse fly out the window.","Then she tried to climb out after it.","His heart nearly stopped.","\"Alpha Killian?\" the driver asked.","\"Box them in and force them onto the shoulder.\"","The driver hit the gas. Their SUV raced forward and pulled alongside Alpha Sebastian’s Bentley. Alpha Killian lowered his window.","For one brief second, Eira met his eyes.","He held her gaze. Trust me.","She seemed to understand. She pulled herself back inside and covered her head.","\"Now,\" Alpha Killian ordered.","The car moved ahead, then cut sharply into the Bentley’s lane. Alpha Sebastian’s driver swerved, but Alpha Killian’s vehicle stayed beside them and pushed them toward the shoulder.","Metal scraped against metal with a violent crash. The Bentley hit the curb and stopped.","Inside, Eira’s seat belt locked across her chest. Her ears rang, but she was not hurt.","\"What the hell was that?\" Alpha Sebastian shouted.","His driver stared into the mirror. \"They forced us off the road.\"","Alpha Killian was already out of his car. His eyes fixed on Eira. He reached her door and pulled the handle.","Locked.","\"Open it,\" he ordered.","Alpha Sebastian leaned across the back seat. \"Get away from my car.\"","Alpha Killian pulled once more. The lock snapped, and the door flew open.","Before Alpha Sebastian could stop him, Alpha Killian released Eira’s seat belt and lifted her out.","\"Alpha Killian Sterling!\"","Alpha Sebastian reached for her, but Alpha Killian turned away and slammed the door in his face.","He carried Eira to the grass beside the road and set her down.","Alpha Sebastian shoved open the other door and climbed out, but Alpha Killian’s driver stepped in front of him.","\"Stay back, Alpha Sebastian.\"","\"You just ran my car off the road!\"","\"And you locked a woman inside it while she was trying to get away. We can talk to the police about both.\"","Alpha Sebastian stopped.","Alpha Killian turned to Eira. \"What the hell were you thinking?\"","\"I told him to pull over.\"","\"So you tried to jump out of a moving car?\"","\"He wouldn’t let me leave.\"","Alpha Killian’s anger did not fade, but his attention shifted. His eyes moved over her face, arms, and legs. \"Are you hurt?\"","\"I don’t think so.\"","He gently turned her wrist. Red marks circled her skin where Alpha Sebastian had grabbed her.","A growl rose in Alpha Killian’s chest.","Eira glanced at the two damaged cars. \"Your car is wrecked.\"","\"It’s a car.\"","\"You hit a Bentley with it.\"","\"I can buy another one.\"","Alpha Killian checked her pupils, then ran his hands carefully over her shoulders to make sure she had no serious injury.","\"Why was he holding you in the car?\"","\"He wanted me to change my statement and stop helping the police.\"","Alpha Killian’s expression hardened.","\"And?\"","\"He told me to apologize to Isabella.\"","For several seconds, Alpha Killian said nothing. Then he looked toward Alpha Sebastian.","The cold in his eyes made even his driver step aside.","Alpha Killian moved in front of Eira, blocking Alpha Sebastian’s path to her.","\"You owe me two dinners now,\" he said quietly.","Despite everything, Eira almost smiled.","--","Alpha Sebastian stormed toward them. \"Eira. Get over here.\"","She stepped out from behind Alpha Killian, but he caught her wrist gently.","His eyes met hers. \"Don’t.\"","Eira stopped. She had only meant to stand beside him, not return to Alpha Sebastian.","Alpha Sebastian did not see the difference. His gaze dropped to Alpha Killian’s hand on her wrist.","\"What the hell do you think you’re doing?\" he demanded. \"You run my car off the road, drag my wife out, and now you won’t let her come to me?\"","Alpha Killian released Eira at once. \"I’m not stopping her.\"","He looked at her instead of Alpha Sebastian. \"If you want to go with him, go.\"","Eira stayed where she was.","The silence hit Alpha Sebastian harder than any answer.","His face darkened.","\"Are you trying to take my wife from me?\"","Alpha Killian stepped between them again.","His expression did not change.","\"And if I am?\""]},{"number":77,"title":"Chapter 77 And If I Am?","paragraphs":["\"And if I am?\"","Alpha Killian glanced at Eira. The wind had blown her hair across her face, and the cold had turned the tip of her nose pink.","He quietly moved to her other side, blocking the wind.","Alpha Sebastian’s face darkened. His wolf bristled at the sight of another Alpha protecting his Luna. A wave of Alpha pressure rolled off him.","Alpha Killian’s own power rose to meet it, cold and controlled. The air between them grew heavy.","\"Careful, Alpha Killian. How would the Sterling board and your pack elders feel about tomorrow’s headline? Sterling Alpha Goes After Another Alpha’s Luna?\"","Alpha Killian smiled.","\"Another Alpha’s Luna? That’s funny. No one even knows you have a Luna.\"","Alpha Sebastian went still.","\"What people do know is that you show up everywhere with Serena Winthrop,\" Alpha Killian continued. \"You took her to the industry gala. You kept her at your side like your future Luna. Half the city already assumes she’ll lead the Hale Pack with you.\"","\"She’s a friend.\"","\"Right. A friend who carries your scent everywhere she goes.\"","Alpha Sebastian’s Alpha pressure sharpened, but Alpha Killian did not so much as blink.","\"Eira will always be my Luna.\"","\"Will she?\"","Eira’s breath caught. \"Alpha Killian.\"","Alpha Killian looked at her. \"Did I get that wrong?\"","She said nothing.","The divorce was still private, and Alpha Sebastian clearly had no idea it was coming.","Alpha Killian turned back to him. \"You hid your Lunafor four years and paraded another she-wolf around in front of every major pack in the city. Now you want to bare your teeth and play the devoted mate. That’s rich.\"","\"Watch your mouth,\" Alpha Sebastian snapped. \"Serena is not my mistress. Eira knows that.\"","Eira gave him a tired look. \"Of course. Just friends. Same story, different day.\"","Relief flashed across Alpha Sebastian’s face. He still thought she believed him.","Alpha Killian almost laughed. \"Alpha Sebastian. A word.\"","He took out his phone and opened a video from the industry gala. The screen showed Alpha Sebastian and Serena alone in a dark corner, kissing.","Alpha Sebastian’s face lost all color. \"Where did you get that?\"","\"Wrong place, wrong time for you. Great timing for me.\"","Alpha Killian raised the volume slightly.","Alpha Sebastian reached for the phone. \"Turn it off.\"","Alpha Killian pulled it out of reach.","\"Let Eira decide where she goes. Stop grabbing her, locking her in cars, and pressuring her to change her police statement.\"","\"And if I don’t?\"","\"She gets the video. So does every business reporter in the city.\"","Alpha Sebastian stared at him.","\"You’d start a public scandal over my Luna?\"","\"No. You started it. I’d just hit send.\"","For several seconds, neither man spoke.","Then Alpha Sebastian lowered his voice.","\"What do you want with her? With your name and money, you could have any woman you wanted.\"","\"That’s none of your business.\"","Alpha Killian held his gaze. \"Your call. Let her go, or explain that video to her and the press.\"","Alpha Sebastian looked toward Eira. She stood several feet away, rubbing the red marks on her wrist.","His expression tightened. \"Where are you taking her?\"","\"Wherever she wants to go.\"","It was not the answer Alpha Sebastian wanted, but he had run out of room to argue.","Alpha Killian signaled to his driver, who called for the Sterling family’s backup car.","A black SUV arrived a few minutes later.","The driver handed Alpha Sebastian a business card. \"Our insurance company will contact you about the Bentley. You can send the repair bill to this number.\"","Alpha Sebastian refused the card. \"I can pay for my own car.\"","\"Good for you,\" Alpha Killian said.","Alpha Sebastian turned to Eira. \"Fine. Keep your statement. Just come home with me.\"","\"I don’t want to go back to the Hale estate.\"","His frustration showed. \"Why not?\"","\"Because I don’t want to.\"","\"That’s not a reason.\"","\"It’s the only one you’re getting.\"","Alpha Killian opened the SUV door and waited.","Eira did not know what Alpha Killian had shown Alpha Sebastian or what the two men had said to each other. She only knew Alpha Sebastian had backed off afterward.","It was not because he respected her choice. Something about Alpha Killian had made him think twice.","People like Alpha Sebastian only backed down when someone with more power pushed back.","Eira got into the SUV. Alpha Killian followed, and the door closed behind them.","As the car pulled away, Alpha Sebastian remained on the shoulder, watching them leave.","\"Thank you,\" Eira said quietly. \"Again. Two dinners don’t begin to cover what I owe you. If there’s ever anything I can do for you, just ask.\"","\"Don’t quit.\"","Eira blinked. \"Except that.\"","Alpha Killian’s expression cooled.","\"I can’t stay,\" she explained. \"This job was always temporary.\"","\"You just said I could ask for anything.\"","\"Anything I can give.\"","Silence filled the SUV.","After a moment, Alpha Killian tried a different approach.","\"You’re making well above the local average. If you leave Alpha Sebastian, that income gives you options. You won’t need his money, and he won’t get to call the shots.\"","Eira went still.","He was not simply talking about a job. He was reminding her that financial freedom could give her a clean break.","Her voice softened. \"Thank you. I mean that.\"","\"So stay.\"","\"No.\"","Alpha Killian turned toward the window.","Stubborn woman.","\"Take us to the Thorne Estate,\" he told the driver.","\"Actually, could you drop me off at Southridge Estates?\" Eira asked.","She and Mrs. Thorne had already discussed the move. The Thorne estate was too far from Sterling Tower and Silix Institute.","Southridge Estates would make everything easier. If Sebastian came looking for her, Mrs. Thorne would let him believe she was still staying at the estate.","Alpha Killian turned to her. \"Southridge?\"","\"It’s nearby.\"","He knew that better than anyone. He lived there.","The SUV entered the gated community, and the security system scanned the vehicle’s tag.","\"Welcome home, Alpha Killian,\" a voice said over the speaker.","Eira looked at Alpha Killian in surprise.","\"You live here?\"","\"At Number One.\" He studied her. \"Where are you going?\"","\"Nine Southridge Lane.\"","The SUV stopped outside Number Nine. Eira entered the security code, waved goodbye, and disappeared into the house.","Alpha Killian watched the door close.","Then he called Miles. \"Run a property search on Nine Southridge Lane.\""]},{"number":78,"title":"Chapter 78 The Truth Slips Out","paragraphs":["At the Hale estate, Luna Margaret was performing an old pack cleansing ritual over Isabella.","She dipped a bundle of juniper and rosemary into salted water, then brushed it over her daughter’s shoulders. The herbs were supposed to clear away bad luck and any hostile scent left by outsiders.","\"That ungrateful girl,\" Luna Margaret muttered. \"After everything this family gave her, she’s still trying to ruin you.\"","Isabella sat on the couch with her arms crossed.","\"Is Eira really still helping the police? Even Sterling House took the settlement and backed off.\"","\"The hotel settled its civil claim,\" Alpha Roger said from behind his newspaper. \"Eira’s statement is still on record.\"","Isabella rolled her eyes.","\"Sebastian will make her change it. He believes me, not her.\"","She gave a smug smile.","\"He said he’d bring her home. When she gets here, she can beg me for forgiveness.\"","\"That’s enough,\" Alpha Roger said. \"Eira will be out of this family soon. Get your apology and move on. Don’t back her into a corner.\"","Luna Margaret had already told him about Eira’s threats.","Alpha Roger did not want her suddenly fighting to stay married just to make the Hales miserable.","Isabella brightened.","\"So you agree Serena should be Sebastian’s Luna?\"","\"Serena is a better match,\" Alpha Roger said. \"She comes from a respected pack, has a strong career, and knows how to carry herself.\"","\"Exactly,\" Luna Margaret said. \"She belongs at Sebastian’s side. Eira never did.\"","\"But Sebastian still hasn’t filed for divorce,\" Isabella complained. \"Serena has been back for a month, and he keeps dragging his feet. If he’d handled it, I wouldn’t have had to step in.\"","Alpha Roger lowered his newspaper.","Luna Margaret stopped brushing the herbs over her.","Isabella was too busy complaining to notice.","\"The drug should’ve knocked Eira out,\" she said. \"I still don’t know how she made it to the bathroom and locked the door. By the time the guy got there, the place was flooded, and he couldn’t do a thing.\"","Luna Margaret’s scent sharpened with alarm.","\"Isabella,\" she warned.","But Isabella kept going.","\"Serena even brought Sebastian upstairs so he’d catch Eira with another man. If it had worked, he would’ve kicked her out on the spot.\"","\"Enough,\" Alpha Roger snapped.","The front door slammed open.","Alpha Sebastian stood in the entrance, his coat hanging from one hand.","A wave of Alpha pressure swept through the room.","Luna Margaret’s herbs trembled in her grip. Isabella’s wolf shrank back at once, and the color drained from her face.","\"S-Sebastian. You’re home.\"","He dropped his coat onto a chair.","\"What did you just say?\"","Isabella scrambled to her feet and moved behind her parents.","\"Nothing. You heard me wrong.\"","Alpha Sebastian crossed the room, his eyes fixed on her.","\"I heard every word.\"","His voice remained quiet, which frightened her more than if he had shouted.","\"The drug. The man. Serena taking me to that room.\" His jaw tightened. \"That was all planned?\"","\"No.\" Isabella shook her head quickly. \"It wasn’t like that.\"","\"Don’t lie to me.\"","His command carried the full weight of an Alpha. Isabella’s wolf fought the order, but her eyes dropped on instinct.","Luna Margaret stepped between them.","\"She made a mistake. Eira is fine, so there’s no reason to tear this family apart over it.\"","Alpha Sebastian turned on her.","\"Eira nearly drowned.\"","\"But she didn’t.\"","He stared at his mother, then looked at Alpha Roger.","\"You both knew?\"","Neither answered.","Disbelief gave way to disgust.","Alpha Sebastian faced his sister again.","\"Isabella Hale.\"","Hearing her full name made her flinch. The last time Alpha Sebastian had used it, she was thirteen and had bullied a younger she-wolf.","He had brought her before the pack council, forced her to apologize in front of the entire pack, and stripped her of every family privilege for three months.","He had been furious then.","Now he stared through his eyes as if Isabella were no longer his sister, but a stranger who had attacked someone under his protection.","\"Sebastian, I only wanted you to divorce her!\" Isabella cried. \"Nobody in this pack wants her here. You love Serena, so why won’t you marry her instead?\"","Luna Margaret grabbed her arm. \"Bella, shut your mouth.\"","Too late.","Alpha Sebastian caught Isabella by the back of her collar and pulled her forward. Alpha pressure crashed through the room, forcing her wolf into submission.","\"Do you have any idea what could’ve happened to Eira?\"","Isabella struggled against his grip.","\"But nothing did! She’s fine.\"","\"She nearly drowned.\"","\"And if your plan had worked?\" Alpha Sebastian demanded. \"What if that man had assaulted her?\"","\"Then you would’ve had a reason to dump her!\"","Alpha Sebastian’s wolf surged so hard that his eyes flashed silver. Alpha Roger started toward them, but Alpha Sebastian’s warning look stopped him.","\"What about what it would’ve done to her?\" Alpha Sebastian asked through clenched teeth.","Isabella’s fear turned into anger.","\"You’ve been married for four years. It’s not like she’s never been with a man.\"","\"Isabella!\" Alpha Roger snapped.","Alpha Sebastian raised his hand.","Then he stopped.","However angry he was, he could not hit his sister. He released her with a hard shove instead.","Isabella rushed behind Alpha Roger, rubbing her neck.","Alpha Sebastian remembered what he had said to Eira in the car. He had demanded that she come home and apologize to the person who had drugged her.","The shame turned his stomach.","\"I’m done cleaning up your messes,\" he said.","Isabella stared at him. \"What?\"","\"I’m not forcing Eira to change her statement.\"","\"But she loves you. She’ll do it if you tell her to.\"","\"Shut up.\"","His Alpha command shook the room. Isabella’s wolf went silent, and she lowered her eyes.","Alpha Sebastian looked around at the comfortable living room and the untouched dinner on the table. His family had been sitting here as if nothing had happened.","\"No wonder she refused to come home,\" he said.","\"Good,\" Luna Margaret replied. \"She never belonged to this pack.\"","Alpha Sebastian turned toward her.","\"She’s my Luna. How is she not part of this family?\"","\"She isn’t one of us,\" Alpha Roger said.","Alpha Sebastian’s expression hardened. \"You feel the same way?\"","Alpha Roger folded his newspaper and set it aside.","\"Answer one question. What do you feel for Eira?\"","Alpha Sebastian went still.","\"And what do you feel for Serena?\" Alpha Roger continued. \"You hide your Luna and parade Serena around like your future Luna. So which woman do you actually want?\"","\"I married Eira,\" Alpha Sebastian said. \"That makes her my responsibility.\"","Alpha Roger held his gaze.","\"That wasn’t the question.\"","Alpha Sebastian’s jaw tightened.","\"I take care of her. I gave her a home, money, everything she needed.\"","\"Again, not what I asked.\"","Alpha Sebastian had no answer.","After a moment, he fell back on the only excuse that still felt safe.","\"A divorce would be bad for Hale Group. It would open our finances to discovery, put years of marital assets on the table, and turn my private life into a public fight.\"","It sounded reasonable. Clean. Businesslike.","But his racing heart told a different story.","The company was not the real reason.","He simply could not stand the thought of Eira walking away."]},{"number":79,"title":"Chapter 79 The Black Stain on Her Record","paragraphs":["\"Fine. I understand.\"","Alpha Roger ended the call.","Alpha Sebastian shot Isabella one last look, grabbed his coat, and walked out.","Isabella watched the door slam behind him.","\"He’s not going to help Eira come after me, is he?\"","\"Of course not,\" Luna Margaret said, taking her hand. \"You’re his blood. Eira has never truly belonged to the Hale Pack.\"","\"But he called her his Luna.\"","\"A marriage contract doesn’t outweigh blood,\" Luna Margaret said firmly. \"He just needs time to cool off.\"","Isabella rubbed the back of her neck. \"He nearly choked me. How am I supposed to smooth that over?\"","Then her eyes lit up.","\"I can’t. But Serena can.\"","She called at once.","\"Serena, Sebastian knows I set Eira up. He’s furious and just stormed out. Can you go find him?\"","She paused, then lowered her voice.","\"Relax. I kept your name out of it.\"","Luna Margaret looked over. \"Kept her name out of what?\"","\"Nothing, Mom.\"","Isabella turned away before Luna Margaret could see her smile.","Alpha Roger went to his study and called Eira. She ignored the first three calls but answered the fourth.","\"What?\"","Alpha Roger’s expression hardened at her tone.","\"Has Sebastian contacted you?\"","\"Yes. I’m not going back, and I have nothing else to say to him.\"","\"So the divorce is still happening?\"","\"That’s the plan.\"","Alpha Roger sat behind his desk.","\"You told Margaret you weren’t asking for money, support, or Hale Group assets. Send me the agreement.\"","\"Why?\"","\"I want to see it for myself.\"","\"You’re not part of the divorce.\"","\"Sebastian is the Alpha of Hale pack. His marriage affects all of us,\" Alpha Roger said. \"If you lied, the family attorneys can tie this up for months.\"","Eira almost laughed. Another threat. The Hales never seemed to have anything else.","\"Hold on.\"","She sent him a copy of the agreement.","Alpha Roger put on his reading glasses and scanned it. Eira had asked for no cash settlement, company shares, or spousal support.","\"Good,\" he said. \"At least you’re not trying to cash in on four years with this family.\"","Eira sat down on the couch at Number Nine.","\"Is that all?\"","\"No. Once the divorce is final, you keep your marriage to Sebastian private. If anyone asks why it ended, you say you grew apart. Nothing about Serena, Isabella, or this family.\"","\"Or what? You’ll sic your lawyers on me?\"","\"Watch your tone, Eira.\"","\"Didn’t Margaret tell you? Threats don’t work on me anymore.\"","Alpha Roger’s Alpha scent sharpened even though no one was there to feel it.","\"You’re getting more disrespectful by the day.\"","\"Must be the Hale influence,\" Eira said. \"Four years around a cheating husband and his criminal sister will do that.\"","\"Eira.\"","\"No need to shout. I heard you.\"","She leaned back against the couch.","\"Don’t worry. I have no plans to advertise the worst decision of my life. I’m just as embarrassed by those four years as you are.\"","She ended the call before Alpha Roger could answer.","--","Eira set her phone facedown on the counter.","The call had left a bad taste in her mouth, but she refused to let the Hales ruin the rest of her evening. This was her house now. Her fresh start. She would rather spend her energy making it feel like home.","She rolled up her sleeves and went back to cleaning.","Number Nine was bigger than she had expected. Most of the furniture was still hidden under dust covers, and several rooms had not been opened in months. It would take more than one afternoon to bring the place back to life.","She had just finished cleaning the living room when her phone rang again.","Mrs. Thorne.","Eira’s hand paused over the screen. After everything that had happened today, a late call from Mrs. Thorne could only mean one thing.","Sebastian had gone looking for her.","\"Mrs. Thorne?\"","\"Sebastian showed up at the estate,\" Mrs. Thorne said. \"He was worked up and kept asking where you were.\"","Eira relaxed slightly. If Alpha Sebastian had told her about the hotel, Mrs. Thorne would not sound this calm.","\"I’m at Number Nine,\" Eira said. \"I’ve been cleaning all afternoon, so I missed his calls.\"","\"I sent him packing and told security not to let him through the gate again,\" Mrs. Thorne said. \"What’s gotten into him?\"","\"I wish I knew. He hasn’t been himself lately.\"","\"Then let him sort himself out. Have you eaten?\"","\"Not yet.\"","\"I figured. I had dinner sent over.\"","Eira smiled. \"Thank you.\"","The doorbell rang seconds after they hung up.","\"That was fast.\"","Eira slipped on her house shoes and went downstairs. She opened the door, expecting a delivery driver.","Alpha Killian stood on the porch with a takeout bag in one hand.","He had changed since that afternoon, but he was still dressed like he had somewhere important to be. His suit was sharp, his tie perfectly straight, and his silver eyes studied her from head to toe.","\"Alpha Killian?\" Eira glanced at his suit. \"Did I forget we had a meeting?\"","\"No.\"","\"I’m not working overtime tonight.\"","Alpha Killian paused, then gave her a tired look.","\"No one asked you to.\"","He held up the bag.","\"Your delivery was waiting at the gate. I saved the driver a trip.\"","\"Oh. Thank you.\"","Eira stepped aside. \"Come in.\"","Alpha Killian entered and looked around. The house was large and well kept, but nearly empty. It did not feel lived in yet.","He sat on the couch.","\"Are you going to offer me something to drink?\"","Eira realized she had left him sitting there without even offering water.","\"Sorry. Tea?\"","\"That works.\"","She went into the kitchen and filled the electric kettle. Plain tea seemed too basic, so she found a jar of dried chamomile from Miss Gwen’s last care package.","As she poured the hot water, her phone lit up on the counter.","Eira, are you still mad?","Another message followed.","I was wrong to ask you to apologize to Isabella.","Eira frowned. Alpha Sebastian had changed his tune fast.","Her phone kept buzzing.","Please pick up.","At least text me so I know you’re okay.","I’m outside the Thorne estate. If you don’t answer, I’ll stay here all night.","Eira’s stomach tightened.","Had Mrs. Thorne’s security team failed to make him leave?","She reached for the phone and knocked the mug off balance.","Hot tea spilled across her slipper.","\"Ah!\"","The cry was barely louder than a breath, but Alpha Killian caught it from the living room.","He was in the kitchen before the mug stopped rolling.","\"What happened?\"","His phone lay forgotten on the couch."]},{"number":80,"title":"Chapter 80 When Sterling Makes His Move","paragraphs":["\"Just a small burn.\"","Eira held her thumb under cool running water, then found the first aid kit beneath the sink. By the time Alpha Killian reached her, she was already applying burn gel.","No panic. No complaints.","She clearly had no trouble taking care of herself.","Alpha Killian pulled out his phone and texted his mother.","[She doesn’t need anyone. What am I supposed to do with that?]","Luna Seraphina replied almost at once.","[Make yourself useful without trying to take over.]","A second message followed.","[And remember, she is still married.]","[Not for long.]","Alpha Killian put away his phone and saw Eira reaching for the gauze.","\"Give me that.\"","\"I can do it.\"","He took the gauze anyway, knelt in front of her, and carefully wrapped her thumb.","Eira watched him in silence.","\"Thank you, Alpha Killian.\"","She started to get up, but he gently pressed her back onto the couch.","\"Sit tight.\"","\"I still owe you tea.\"","\"I think I can manage.\" Alpha Killian returned with the kettle, two mugs, and the old plastic jar from the counter. He turned it over in his hand.","\"This jar has seen better days.\"","\"It came from the orphanage. \"Eira quickly took it from him.","Alpha Killian caught the change in her expression. \"I meant the container.\"","\"I know.\" She still held it tightly.","Alpha Killian held out his hand. \"Truce?\"","After a moment, she handed it back.","He opened the lid. The scent of elderflower and wild mint drifted into the room. His wolf stirred, then slowly settled.","\"This is a calming blend,\" he said.","\"Miss Gwen used to make it for the younger wolves when they had trouble controlling their first shifts.\"","\"And for you?\"","\"I don’t have a wolf, but she never left me out.\"","Alpha Killian looked at her.","Eira’s tone was casual, but he heard what she had not said. She had grown up surrounded by young wolves and pack traditions she could never fully share.","He added a small pinch to each mug.","\"Easy,\" she warned. \"That has to last until next fall.\"","Alpha Killian stopped at once.","\"You only get one jar a year?\"","\"The kids gather the herbs on the hills behind the orphanage. Miss Gwen dries them and makes a jar for everyone who has moved away.\"","Alpha Killian handed her a mug.","\"So it’s a pack tradition.\"","Eira shook her head. \"More like a family tradition.\"","Something in Alpha Killian’s chest tightened.","They sat across from each other as the herbs steeped. The warm scent filled the empty house, making it feel a little less cold.","\"We used to race to see who could fill a basket first,\" Eira said. \"The wolf kids cheated. They could smell the best patches from half a mile away.\"","\"What did you do?\"","\"I followed them.\"","Alpha Killian raised an eyebrow.","\"Then I got there first and took the best ones.\"","A quiet laugh escaped him. \"Smart.\"","\"They called it cheating.\"","\"They were using wolf senses against you. All you did was even the odds.\"","Eira looked at him over the rim of her mug. \"That’s exactly what I told them.\"","Her scent softened again.","Alpha Killian’s wolf relaxed, pleased that she no longer seemed ready to hide behind her walls.","\"We picked yarrow too,\" she added. \"Miss Gwen kept it for cuts and injuries.\"","Alpha Killian waited for her to continue.","When she did not, he asked, \"And?\"","\"And what?\"","\"What happened with the yarrow?\"","Eira gave him a strange look. \"This isn’t story time.\"","\"Could’ve fooled me.\"","A faint smile touched her lips.","Alpha Sebastian had always treated her childhood like something she should forget. Alpha Killian simply listened. To him, the memories mattered because they belonged to her.","The doorbell rang before she could say more.","Dinner from Mrs. Thorne had arrived.","Eira brought the bags inside and found Alpha Killian still on the couch, making no move to leave.","\"Have you eaten?\"","\"No.\"","\"You planning to stick around?\"","Alpha Killian leaned back. \"Depends. Are you inviting me?\"","\"There’s plenty.\" She carried the bags toward the dining room. \"You might as well stay.\"","--","During dinner, Eira checked her phone.","Another message from Alpha Sebastian waited on the screen.","[If you don’t answer, I’m staying outside the Thorne estate all night.]","Her jaw tightened. Mrs. Thorne had already sent him away once, yet he was still hanging around and making a scene.","Eira opened the spare number she used for private matters and texted Serena.","[Alpha Sebastian is outside the Thorne estate. You should go get him before he spends the whole night there.]","Serena replied almost at once.","[Who is this?]","Eira muted the conversation and returned to her dinner. Serena would figure out the rest. She always did when Alpha Sebastian was involved.","Across the table, Alpha Killian watched her set down the phone.","\"You cooked for Lila.\"","Eira looked up. \"She helped me with something.\"","\"I’ve helped you twice.\"","There was no missing his point.","Eira held back a smile. \"Are you asking me to cook for you?\"","\"I’m saying it would be fair.\"","\"All right. What do you like?\"","\"Surprise me.\"","\"That’s not very helpful.\"","\"I’m not picky.\"","His wolf clearly disagreed. It had already decided anything made by Eira would do.","\"I’ll figure something out,\" she said.","Alpha Killian finished the rest of his dinner without rushing. Afterward, he helped carry the empty containers to the kitchen, then put on his coat.","Eira walked him to the door.","\"Thank you for stopping by.\"","Alpha Killian glanced at her bandaged thumb. \"Try not to injure yourself again tonight.\"","\"I’ll do my best.\"","\"And don’t answer the door for Hale.\"","\"I wasn’t planning to.\"","Alpha Killian gave a satisfied nod and stepped outside.","Once he reached Number One, he pulled out his phone and opened his mother’s contact.","Luna Seraphina’s advice had worked. He had helped without taking over, stayed for dinner, and secured another invitation.","After a moment, he changed her contact name to: Strategic Advisor","--","Serena found Alpha Sebastian parked across from the Thorne estate in a borrowed sedan, smoking behind the wheel.","She opened the passenger door and slid inside.","\"Sebastian?\"","He kept his eyes on the estate gates.","Serena glanced around the unfamiliar car. \"Where’s your Bentley?\"","\"Wrecked.\"","Her eyes widened. \"What happened?\"","\"Alpha Killian Sterling happened.\"","Earlier that evening, Alpha Killian had forced his car off the road and taken Eira with him. The memory made Alpha Sebastian’s wolf pace beneath his skin.","He took another drag and flicked the ash out the window.","Serena frowned. \"Since when do you smoke?\"","\"Since you left.\"","His answer came too quickly.","Alpha Sebastian looked down at the cigarette. He had started smoking after Serena walked away years ago, but he had quit after his mating ceremony with Eira.","Eira hated the smell.","For four years, he had not touched a single cigarette.","Until tonight."]},{"number":81,"title":"Chapter 81 We Need To Keep Our Distance","paragraphs":["\"Sebastian.\"","Serena reached for his hand as he crushed the cigarette in the ashtray.","\"Why are you here?\" he asked.","\"Your parents called. Isabella is scared, and I’ve been worried sick.\"","She checked his fingers for burns, then brushed her thumb along his jaw.","\"Please don’t start smoking again.\"","Her familiar scent filled the car. Once, it would have calmed his wolf without fail.","Serena closed her eyes and leaned closer.","Just before their lips met, Alpha Sebastian turned away.","A strange panic tightened his chest.","He loved Serena. He had waited years for her. He had never even slept with Eira because part of him had always belonged to Serena.","So why had he pulled back?","The video Alpha Killian had shown him flashed through his mind. If it got out, Serena would be branded as the woman who broke up an Alpha’s marriage. Her career and her chance of becoming a respected Luna would take a serious hit.","That had to be the reason.","He was protecting her.","Serena opened her eyes. Her scent turned sharp with hurt.","\"We need to keep our distance,\" Alpha Sebastian said.","She went still. \"You don’t want me anymore.\"","A tear rolled down her cheek.","\"That’s not it.\" Alpha Sebastian wiped it away. \"Someone recorded us kissing at the gala. If that video gets out, the press will tear you apart.\"","\"Then you should...\"","Divorce her.","The words almost slipped out.","Serena swallowed them.","If she pushed too hard, Alpha Sebastian might finally ask himself why he could not let Eira go. Serena had already seen the way his wolf reacted to his wife. He called it duty and possessiveness, but she knew better.","She could not afford to make him see it too.","Alpha Sebastian was no longer the ambitious young executive she had left behind. He now ran Hale Group and stood next in line to lead the Hale Pack. He had money, influence, and a future most women in their circle would fight for.","Serena had not come back to lose him to the wife she once considered temporary.","She lowered her eyes and made her voice shake.","\"So that’s it? You’re cutting me loose because I left?\"","\"Serena, no.\"","\"My grandfather sent me overseas. I didn’t have a choice.\"","\"I know.\"","Alpha Sebastian remembered the night he had planned to tell Serena how he felt.","She disappeared before he got the chance. No warning. No goodbye. Hours later, a mutual friend told him she had left California.","He had thought he would never see her again.","When Serena finally reached out, he forgave her. After that, he flew overseas for her birthday every year. He paid for her apartment, supported her career, and waited for her to come home.","Serena saw his expression soften and pressed her advantage.","\"Don’t walk away from me now,\" she whispered. \"You promised you never would.\"","Her flower-sweet scent filled the car, familiar enough to stir his wolf.","\"You’re the only man I’ve ever loved. The only man I’ve ever been with.\"","Alpha Sebastian’s hands tightened around the steering wheel.","He remembered the night they had crossed that line. They had both been drinking, but he had never regretted it.","\"If you’re worried being with me will ruin both our reputations,\" Serena continued, \"I don’t care.\"","The truth was, she cared more about her own reputation than she would ever admit. But she could not let him pull away now.","If she could no longer push him toward divorce, she would have to deal with Eira herself.","\"Serena,\" he said, his voice softening.","\"I’m here. I’m not leaving you again.\"","Another tear slipped down her cheek.","Alpha Sebastian wiped it away.","\"Just give me time.\"","The same promise he had made for years.","Serena leaned into his palm. \"Okay.\"","She tried to kiss him again.","Alpha Sebastian turned his face away, but this time he pulled her into his arms.","It was not what Serena wanted, but she let it go. She had something more important to find out.","\"What happened with Isabella?\" she asked. \"Was the hotel incident really a misunderstanding?\"","Alpha Sebastian released her.","\"No. Isabella planned the whole thing.\"","Serena went cold.","\"How do you know?\"","\"I heard her admit it.\" He rubbed a hand over his face. \"She drugged Eira and arranged for that man to enter the room.\"","Serena watched him carefully. \"Did she say anything else?\"","\"Like what?\"","\"Nothing. I mean, what did you do?\"","\"I told her I was done covering for her.\"","His gaze returned to the Thorne estate gates.","\"Before I knew the truth, I tried to force Eira to change her statement. I even told her to apologize to Isabella.\"","His wolf shifted with shame. \"I failed her.\"","Serena’s stomach tightened. The plan had not only failed. It had made Alpha Sebastian feel guilty about Eira.","\"Don’t beat yourself up,\" she said gently. \"You believed your sister. Anyone would.\"","\"I should’ve believed my wife.\"","The answer caught Serena off guard.","She hid her anger behind a soft smile.","\"Eira will come around. Family forgives family.\"","Alpha Sebastian said nothing.","\"And Isabella was wrong,\" Serena added quickly. \"There’s no excuse for what she did. Still, Eira is safe. Thanks to Alpha Killian.\"","She let his name hang between them.","\"He found her right away, carried her out, and stayed through her treatment.\" Serena paused. \"That’s a lot for an Alpha to do for an employee.\"","Alpha Sebastian’s jaw tightened.","Serena lowered her voice.","\"Do you think Alpha Killian has feelings for YOUR Luna?\"","\"Impossible.\" Alpha Sebastian frowned. \"Killian is the Alpha to one of the oldest packs in the country. Why would he be interested in someone like Eira? Besides, he knows she’s married to me.\"","He folded his arms.","\"He’s using her to get under my skin. That’s all.\"","Serena gave him a doubtful look. \"Why would he bother?\"","\"Because we’re fighting for the same ground in the tech industry.\"","Sterling Group was a corporate giant, but Sterling Tech was still a new branch.","Hale Group had spent more than a decade building its name in the industry, with money and political support from the Carter Pack.","The Carter Group was a first-tier pack with deep ties to several regional councils. Their alliance with the Hales gave Alpha Sebastian access to investors, government contracts, and talented young wolves from across the country.","In the human world, it looked like corporate backing.","Among wolves, everyone knew what it really was. Two packs protecting the same territory.","\"It’s an Alpha power play,\" Alpha Sebastian said. \"He wants me off balance.\""]},{"number":82,"title":"Chapter 82 Deflection and Delusion","paragraphs":["Serena’s smile turned bitter. \"Is that really what you think?\"","She could believe Alpha Killian had no interest in Eira. But using another Alpha’s Luna as bait sounded more like an excuse Alpha Sebastian had made up to protect his pride.","\"Yes,\" he said firmly.","Serena changed the subject. \"Did you come here to see Eira?\"","Alpha Sebastian looked toward the gates. \"I wanted to apologize. She won’t see me.\"","His shoulders sagged.","Alpha Sebastian Hale had always been the golden boy of the Hale Pack. Sharp, driven, and impossible to shake.","Serena had only seen him lose control once before, when she left California.","Now Eira was having the same effect on him.","That scared her.","\"Why is she staying here?\" Serena asked. \"This neighborhood isn’t exactly cheap.\"","\"It belongs to her late mentor’s widow.\"","Alpha Sebastian paused. \"Eira worked hard in school. She earned a master’s degree, but she never went for a doctorate. Now she has an admin job at Sterling Tower.\"","Serena glanced at the estate again.","For a moment, she wondered who Eira’s mentor had been. This estate was worth a fortune.","If Crawford’s research reached the market, the patents alone could be worth far more than this house.","Could the property be connected to Dr. Crawford?","But Dr. Crawford was believed to be young, not the elderly widow Alpha Sebastian had described.","It was probably nothing.","Serena leaned closer and smiled. \"You never say anything bad about Eira. That’s interesting.\"","Alpha Sebastian glanced at her. \"What about me?\"","\"You’re exceptional,\" he replied automatically. \"You’re doing serious research and producing real results. Not many people can do that.\"","\"And you’re incredible too,\" Serena said. \"You didn’t inherit your position. You fought your way to the top. That must have cost you a lot.\"","Alpha Sebastian went still.","Eira had said almost the same thing when he became president of Hale Group.","\"Sebastian?\" Serena’s voice pulled him back.","\"It’s nothing.\" But his scent had changed. Regret had slipped through his usual Alpha control.","Serena knew at once that he had been thinking about Eira.","She could not let him sit outside the estate all night, turning guilt into something deeper.","Serena suddenly gasped and pressed a hand to her stomach.","Alpha Sebastian turned to her. \"What’s wrong?\"","\"I don’t know. It hurts.\"","Her face tightened as if another cramp had hit.","\"I think I need a doctor.\"","Alpha Sebastian’s attention shifted to her at once. He started the car and drove away from the estate.","At a nearby hospital, the tests came back normal.","\"It’s probably related to your cycle,\" the doctor said. \"Rest, drink plenty of water, and come back if it gets worse.\"","Serena noticed the relief on Alpha Sebastian’s face.","Her period was not due for another two weeks. Still, if it failed to come, she might be able to use that.","As they left the exam room, she leaned against his arm.","\"Could you make me some ginger tea when we get home?\"","\"I want cinnamon bread pudding,\" Alpha Sebastian said absently.","Serena stopped.","\"What?\"","Alpha Sebastian froze.","That had nothing to do with her request.","He had been thinking about Eira again.","--","Meanwhile, Eira decided to cook Alpha Killian a proper thank-you dinner.","Since he had only told her to surprise him, she texted Lila.","Eira: What does your brother like to eat? I’m making him dinner to thank him.","Lila called seconds later.","\"So he actually talked you into cooking for him?\"","\"He helped me twice.\"","\"And dinner was his price?\" Lila laughed. \"What a wimp.\"","Eira frowned. \"What does that mean?\"","\"Nothing. My brother’s a pain in the ass when it comes to food. I’ll get you a list from our chef.\"","\"Could you put it in a spreadsheet?\"","\"Of course you’d ask for a spreadsheet.\"","\"It’s more efficient.\"","\"Fine. I’ll drop it off later.\"","Lila ended the call and drove to the Sterling Manor.","She found the family chef in the kitchen and opened a new spreadsheet on her tablet.","\"Give me the basics. What will Alpha Killian eat, and what won’t he touch?\"","The chef raised an eyebrow. \"Why do you care?\"","\"I don’t. Eira does.\"","A knowing smile crossed his face. \"So that’s where this is going.\"","Lila narrowed her eyes. \"What do you know?\"","\"Only that your mother threatened to divorce your father if he cost her a future Luna Sterling.\"","Lila burst out laughing, then stopped.","\"Wait. What did Dad do?\"","\"He approved the Hale settlement after the incident at Sterling House.\"","\"What incident?\"","The chef gave her the short version.","By the time he finished, Lila’s smile was gone.","She grabbed the tablet and stormed out.","--","Sterling Group","Alpha Killian was in a strategy meeting down the hall, leaving Eira alone in his office to organize the files on his side desk.","She had been kept away from active projects because her position was temporary.","In less than two weeks, she would be gone.","The office door suddenly flew open.","\"Eira!\"","Eira looked up.","Lila stood in the doorway, her eyes red and her scent sharp with anger.","\"Why didn’t you tell me what happened at Sterling House?\"","Eira went still.","\"I had to hear it from our chef,\" Lila continued. \"I thought we were friends.\"","\"We are.\"","\"Then why didn’t you call me?\"","Eira crossed the room and pulled her into a hug.","\"I’m sorry.\"","Lila held on to her.","\"You didn’t do anything wrong. I just want you to know you don’t have to handle everything alone.\" Her wolf stirred protectively beneath her skin. \"I can raise hell. I can throw a punch. And if that doesn’t work, my last name usually does.\"","A small smile touched Eira’s lips.","\"I’ll call you next time.\"","\"Good. Call in the cavalry.\"","\"You’re the cavalry?\"","\"No.\" Lila pulled back and wiped her eyes. \"That would be my brother. I’m more of a warning shot.\"","She handed Eira her tablet.","\"Here’s the list you asked for. Every food Killian won’t touch.\"","Eira glanced at the long spreadsheet. \"There are six tabs.\"","\"I told you he was picky. Honestly, give him water and tell him dinner’s canceled.\"","\"Still trashing me behind my back?\"","Alpha Killian’s voice came from the doorway.","Lila spun around. He had returned from the meeting and stood with his arms folded.","His expression was cold, but his wolf relaxed when it caught Eira’s calm scent. She was safe.","\"I’m helping,\" Lila said.","\"You’re doing a great job.\"","She could hear the sarcasm.","Her phone buzzed before she could fire back. Professor Chase was calling.","\"I need to take this.\"","Lila stepped into the hall.","\"Professor?\"","\"I just emailed you several papers,\" Professor Chase said. \"They’re all by the same researcher. Her approach to chip architecture may help with your prototype.\"","\"I’ll read them tonight.\"","\"Don’t just skim them. Study the models. This researcher is the real deal.\"","\"Got it. Thanks.\"","Lila ended the call and opened the first paper.","Alpha Killian stepped into the hall behind her.","\"Who was that?\"","Lila jumped. \"Seriously? Ever heard of personal space?\"","\"You were standing outside my office.\"","\"Professor Chase sent me some papers. Happy?\"","Alpha Killian glanced at her screen.","The paper focused on a new chip architecture that could lower energy use without reducing processing speed. The work was advanced enough to hold his attention at once.","Then he saw the author’s name.","Eira...","His gaze sharpened."]},{"number":83,"title":"Chapter 83 The Hidden Prodigy?","paragraphs":["Lila snatched her phone back.","\"Hold on.\"","Alpha Killian took it again and enlarged the author line.","Eira Crawford","He read it twice before looking through the open office door.","Eira sat at her desk, calmly sorting files as if nothing had happened.","Lila followed his gaze. Then she looked at the paper again.","\"No way.\"","Her surprise quickly turned into excitement.","\"Do you think that’s our Eira?\"","\"Where did you get this?\" Alpha Killian asked.","\"Professor Chase sent it. My chip prototype bombed, so he gave me a reading list.\"","\"Which journal?\"","\"Nature Computational Science.\"","Alpha Killian’s attention sharpened.","The journal was one of the most respected publications in the field. The paper was not a student project or a minor lab report. Whoever wrote it was an expert.","Lila stared at Alpha Killian. \"That can’t be a coincidence.\"","\"Ask her.\"","\"Why me?\"","\"You’re the one dying to know.\"","\"You want to know too.\"","Alpha Killian gave her a look.","Lila rolled her eyes and walked into the office.","She dropped into the chair beside Eira and held out her phone.","\"Okay, I need a straight answer.\"","Eira glanced at the screen. Recognition flashed across her face, but it disappeared almost at once.","\"What about it?\"","\"The author is Eira Crawford.\" Lila leaned closer. \"Please tell me you’ve secretly been a genius this whole time.\"","Eira remained calm. \"It isn’t me.\"","\"Seriously?\"","\"Seriously.\"","Lila pointed to the affiliation. \"Then how do you explain this?\"","Eira handed the phone back. \"Crawford isn’t exactly a rare last name.\"","\"Eira isn’t exactly common.\"","\"No, but it isn’t unique either.\"","Lila studied her face.","Eira did not look nervous. Her voice stayed steady.","\"Are you sure?\" Lila asked.","\"If I could publish work like that, would I be organizing expense reports in your brother’s office?\"","That was hard to argue with.","Lila sighed. \"Fine. Same name. Weird coincidence.\"","She glanced toward the doorway. \"For the record, Killian made me ask.\"","Eira looked up. \"He did?\"","\"Yep.\"","That concerned her more than Lila’s questions.","Alpha Killian knew Professor Thorne had created the project Sterling Tech was trying to acquire.","Now he had seen a major paper written by an Eira Crawford.","He would not miss that connection.","Lila texted him in full view of Eira.","[Not her. Same name.]","His reply arrived seconds later.","[Okay.]","Lila held up the screen. \"See? Case closed.\"","Eira looked toward the doorway.","Alpha Killian was already gone. He had not asked another question.","That meant he believed her. For now.","Eira lowered her eyes and returned to the file in front of her.","The rest of the day passed quietly, but Alpha Sebastian kept blowing up Eira’s phone.","She finally muted him.","When she left Sterling Tower that evening, she spotted his borrowed sedan near the main entrance. She turned around, slipped out through the parking garage, and called a rideshare.","Once she was safely on her way to Southridge Estates, she texted him.","[I’m already at Mrs. Thorne’s. Don’t come.]","Alpha Sebastian drove there anyway. Security stopped him at the gate.","He hit the steering wheel and grabbed his phone.","[Do you really have to shut me out like this?]","[How long are you going to stay mad?]","[Can we talk after you cool off?]","Too tired to argue, Eira sent one word.","[Fine.]","It was vague enough to get him off her back for the night.","Over the next few days, Alpha Sebastian stayed away from the Hale estate. He also froze Isabella’s allowance.","Alpha Roger and Luna Margaret blamed Eira for both.","\"What else do you want from this family?\"","\"How long are you going to keep this up?\"","Eira hung up on them.","Her attorney had more useful information.","\"The police investigation is still open,\" he told her. \"But without a clean chain of evidence connecting Isabella to the drug and the man at the hotel, it may stall.\"","\"So she gets away with it?\"","\"Criminal charges are up to the police and the district attorney. You can still move forward with a civil claim, but it could take time.\"","He paused.","\"At this point, the main benefit may be keeping pressure on the Hales.\"","Later, Eira told Lila what he had said.","Lila’s eyes lit up. \"Keeping them miserable sounds like a solid benefit to me.\"","\"It could drag on for months.\"","\"Good. Let Bella sweat.\"","Eira gave her a look. \"She’ll burn the whole place down before she admits she was wrong.\"","\"Probably.\" Lila grinned. \"But if she ever comes crawling over here with an apology, let me handle it.\"","\"You have a plan?\"","\"I always have a plan.\"","Eira smiled. \"Fine. She’s all yours.\"","Lila suddenly sat up straighter. \"Speaking of plans, you’re cooking for Killian tomorrow, right?\"","\"Yes.\"","\"Can I come?\"","\"Ask him.\"","Lila sent a message.","Alpha Killian replied almost at once.","[No.]","She stared at the screen. \"Wow. Not even a fake excuse.\"","\"Want me to try?\"","\"Yes. Maybe he’ll act human for you.\"","Eira texted him.","[Can Lila join us for dinner tomorrow?]","His answer came just as quickly.","[No.]","Lila groaned. \"Okay. That’s a hard no.\"","She said. \"What are you making? I’ll have the groceries delivered. Southridge is in the middle of nowhere, and you don’t have a car.\"","\"I’ll send you a list, but I’m paying.\"","\"Deal.\"","Lila put away her phone, then gave Eira a wounded look. \"I’m still salty that you wouldn’t stay at one of my places.\"","\"What would make you feel better?\"","\"Let me crash here tonight.\"","Eira laughed. \"All right.\"","\"That was way too easy.\"","\"You’re my friend. You don’t need an excuse.\"","Lila’s teasing smile softened.","Most of the women she knew from powerful packs spent their time at charity events, art shows, or family businesses. Very few worked in a lab. The ones who tried to get close to her usually wanted access to the Sterling name.","Eira never asked for anything.","\"I don’t have many real friends,\" Lila admitted.","\"Neither do I.\"","\"Great. Two antisocial lab rats. We’re a perfect match.\"","They spent the night at Number Nine, talking long after they should have gone to sleep.","--","The next morning, Eira woke to a message from Rachel.","[Everyone checked in. Class is ready.]","Across town, the same class reminder appeared on Alpha Sebastian’s phone.","He grabbed his keys and headed out.","If Eira would not take his calls, he would wait for her after class."]},{"number":84,"title":"Chapter 84 Does Alpha Killian Know His Way Around?","paragraphs":["The groceries arrived that morning. By noon, Eira’s fridge was stocked with everything she needed for a proper American-style dinner.","Ribeye steaks. Jumbo shrimp. Asparagus. Potatoes.","Surf and turf seemed like a safe bet. Lila’s spreadsheet said Alpha Killian liked good steak, fresh seafood, and simple food without heavy sauces.","Eira texted him.","Dinner at my place. Seven tonight. Don’t be late.","His reply came at once.","I won’t.","She sent one more message.","Can you bring my suitcase?","Sure.","At six thirty, the doorbell rang.","Eira rinsed the shrimp off her hands and opened the door. Alpha Killian stood outside in a charcoal suit, holding a bottle of Napa Cabernet and a box from a local bakery.","\"You’re early,\" she said.","\"I brought wine and dessert. That buys me thirty minutes.\"","Eira stepped aside. His clean cedar scent followed him into the house, making her strangely aware of how quiet Number Nine was.","She looked toward the driveway.","\"Where’s my suitcase?\"","Alpha Killian stopped.","\"I forgot it.\"","\"You had one job.\"","A flicker of amusement crossed his face. \"I’ll bring it next time.\"","Eira did not notice how smoothly he had created a reason to return.","\"Fine. Make yourself comfortable. I’m still working on dinner.\"","Alpha Killian set down the wine and bakery box. Instead of sitting, he took off his jacket, rolled up his sleeves, and followed her into the kitchen.","\"What are you doing?\" Eira asked.","\"Pitching in.\"","\"You’re my guest.\"","\"And you’re cooking enough food for a football team.\"","\"I didn’t know how much an Alpha eats.\"","His wolf liked that answer far too much.","Alpha Killian looked over the counter. The steaks were resting, the potatoes were boiling, and the shrimp still needed to be peeled.","\"Put me to work.\"","\"Can you cook?\"","\"I can hold my own.\"","Eira handed him the shrimp. \"Peel and devein these.\"","Alpha Killian got to work without hesitation. His movements were quick and clean.","Eira watched him finish the first shrimp.","\"Well, look at you.\"","\"Try not to sound so shocked.\"","\"Where did you learn that?\"","\"My dad.\" That was all he said.","Eira nodded and turned back to the stove.","Alpha Killian waited.","When she said nothing else, he looked over. \"That’s it? You’re not going to ask?\"","\"You clearly don’t want to talk about it.\"","\"I said my dad taught me. I didn’t say it was classified.\"","Eira gave him a puzzled look.","Alpha Killian sighed and returned to the shrimp.","His flirting was getting absolutely nowhere.","--","With Alpha Killian helping, dinner came together fast.","He peeled the shrimp, trimmed the asparagus, and handed Eira whatever she needed before she asked. They moved around the kitchen with surprising ease, almost like they had done this before.","By six forty-five, the ribeyes were resting on the counter. The garlic butter shrimp, roasted asparagus, and mashed potatoes were ready.","Only the burrata salad was left.","Eira placed the cheese in the center of the plate, then began folding thin slices of prosciutto into small roses.","Halfway through, she stopped.","She had learned that trick for Alpha Sebastian. He liked his food arranged that way, so she had spent an entire afternoon practicing until every fold looked perfect.","\"Something wrong?\" Alpha Killian asked.","\"No.\"","Eira pulled the prosciutto apart and laid the slices around the burrata in a simple circle.","Alpha Killian noticed, but he did not ask.","\"All set?\"","\"All set.\"","He picked up the platter and carried it to the dining room.","Eira watched him go.","In four years, Alpha Sebastian had never once helped her in the kitchen. He had never carried a plate or asked if she needed a hand.","Alpha Killian had walked in, rolled up his sleeves, and made himself useful.","Eira took off her apron and followed him.","She remembered the fruit basket and reached for it at the same time Alpha Killian did. Their fingers brushed.","Eira quickly pulled her hand back.","\"I’ve got it,\" Alpha Killian said.","He washed the fruit and brought it back in a serving bowl. When he returned, Eira was pouring the wine.","They sat down a few minutes before seven.","Alpha Killian cut into the ribeye first. The center was warm and pink, exactly medium rare.","\"Lila’s spreadsheet said that’s how you like it,\" Eira said.","\"So that’s what she brought you. My entire food profile.\"","\"She was very thorough.\"","\"I’m sure she enjoyed collecting classified information.\"","Eira almost smiled. \"How is it?\"","Alpha Killian took another bite before answering.","\"Worth the wait.\"","Eira relaxed. \"Good. Then we’re even.\"","Alpha Killian looked up. \"Who said we were even?\"","\"You asked for dinner. I made dinner.\"","\"I helped.\"","\"That was your choice.\"","His mouth curved slightly. \"Then I guess you still owe me.\"","Eira stared at him, trying to decide whether he was serious.","Alpha Killian calmly reached for the shrimp.","Her phone buzzed before she could answer. An unread message from Rachel had been sitting there since earlier that day.","[Morning session finished. Everyone checked out.]","Eira locked the screen and set the phone facedown.","--","At the same time, Alpha Sebastian checked his watch.","Right on time.","He grabbed a bouquet of roses and a small jewelry box from the passenger seat, then walked into the preconception wellness clinic.","The receptionist looked up. Her eyes briefly widened at his tailored suit and expensive watch.","\"Hi. Can I help you?\"","\"I’m here to pick up my wife.\" Alpha Sebastian gave her his most charming smile. \"Eira Hale. I’m Sebastian.\"","The receptionist checked the pickup note on her screen.","\"Mr. Hale. Yes, the class should be wrapping up now.\"","She handed him a bottle of water and pointed toward the waiting area.","\"You can take a seat.\"","\"Thanks.\"","Alpha Sebastian sat facing the hallway, the roses resting beside him. A few minutes later, women began leaving the classroom.","Then he spotted a familiar figure.","Long golden hair. Slim build. Face mask.","The woman glanced at her phone as she walked, then rolled her neck as if she had been sitting too long. A name badge hung against her jacket, but her hair covered most of it.","Alpha Sebastian stood and picked up the flowers.","The receptionist followed his gaze and smiled.","\"Mrs. Hale, your husband is here.\"","The masked woman stopped cold.","\"Excuse me?\"","Alpha Sebastian walked toward her, his voice warm and confident.","\"Eira.\""]},{"number":85,"title":"Chapter 85 The Kind of Handsome Man Who Turns Out to Be Rotten","paragraphs":["Halfway through dinner, Eira’s phone buzzed.","A text from Rachel flashed across the screen.","[Your husband is here!]","Eira set down her fork.","\"Excuse me, Alpha Killian.\"","She stepped away from the table and answered Rachel’s call.","\"What happened?\"","\"Your husband showed up with flowers,\" Rachel whispered. \"The receptionist called me Mrs. Hale right in front of him. I ducked into the restroom, but he’s waiting outside. What am I supposed to do?\"","Eira opened Alpha Sebastian’s messages. He had asked several times if she was having cramps and whether she still planned to attend class.","When she failed to answer, he must have decided to surprise her.","\"Stay where you are,\" Eira said. \"Keep quiet and don’t come out until I call.\"","\"What about Sebastian?\"","\"I’ll handle him.\"","Eira ended the call and returned to the table.","\"I’m sorry, but something came up. I have to go.\"","Alpha Killian set down his fork. \"What happened?\"","\"It’s complicated.\"","\"Try me.\"","Eira checked the time. She had no room to argue.","\"Sebastian signed me up for a fertility class. I hired someone to check in for me, and he just showed up there with flowers. She’s hiding in the restroom.\"","Alpha Killian stared at her.","\"You hired a stand-in for fertility class?\"","\"Yes.\"","A hint of amusement touched his eyes, but it disappeared quickly.","\"And now you’re running over there to save her.\"","\"I have to get her out before Sebastian figures it out.\"","Alpha Killian’s expression cooled. \"You’re still worried about keeping him happy?\"","\"No. I’m trying to keep the divorce simple.\"","Eira grabbed her purse.","\"If he learns I’ve been faking the classes, he’ll use it to start another fight. He could drag out the divorce, demand more financial records, and make the whole thing a nightmare.\"","The Sovereign Processor project was close to moving forward. If the divorce stalled until the money started coming in, Alpha Sebastian might try to claim part of it as marital income.","She would not let her work bankroll the Hales or Serena.","\"I can’t hand him ammunition,\" she said.","Alpha Killian stood and reached for his jacket.","\"I’ll drive you.\"","Eira stopped him.","\"You can’t.\"","\"Why not?\"","\"Sebastian already thinks you’re using me to get at him. If I show up in your car, he’ll lose it.\"","Alpha Killian gave a short, humorless laugh. His Alpha scent sharpened.","\"So now I’m supposed to hide because Hale can’t control his wolf?\"","\"I’m asking you not to turn a bad situation into a pack challenge.\"","For a moment, neither moved.","Then Alpha Killian sat back down.","\"Fine.\"","\"Thank you. And I’m sorry about dinner.\"","Eira hurried toward the door.","Alpha Killian watched her leave, his wolf pacing beneath his skin.","She had cooked him a full meal, only to run off and clean up another mess Alpha Sebastian had made.","He was getting tired of watching Hale take priority, even when Eira claimed he no longer mattered.","---","In the rideshare, Eira texted Alpha Sebastian to buy herself time.","[My period started. I wasn’t prepared, and I bled through my clothes.]","[Can you grab these pads for me?]","She attached a photo.","His reply came a minute later.","[I’ll ask the front desk.]","Eira’s stomach dropped. Of course he had to play the perfect husband.","[They won’t have this brand. The others give me a rash. Please just go to the drugstore.]","After a short pause, he replied.","[You never ask me for things like this.]","Then another message followed.","[I’m glad you finally feel like you can.]","Eira ignored the comment.","[Will you get them or not?]","[Yeah. There’s a CVS down the street. I’m heading there now.]","[Thanks.]","That bought her ten minutes. Maybe fifteen.","The moment her rideshare stopped outside the clinic, Eira put on a mask and hurried inside. Alpha Sebastian was gone.","She went straight to the women’s restroom and knocked on the last stall.","\"It’s me.\"","Rachel opened the door and exhaled hard.","\"Thank God. I thought I was toast.\"","\"Keep your voice down. We need to switch jackets.\"","They traded coats. Rachel pulled her hair into a ponytail and removed her mask. Eira let her own hair fall loose, then zipped Rachel’s jacket high enough to hide her clothes.","Rachel looked her over. \"Why are we pulling a whole Mission: Impossible routine? Can’t you just tell your husband you’re done with the class?\"","\"He won’t take no for an answer.\"","\"That bad?\"","\"He’s sleeping with someone else, and he still expects me to have his baby.\"","Rachel stared at her.","\"What a dirtbag.\"","\"Exactly.\"","Eira adjusted her mask.","\"You leave. I’ll meet him in the lobby and get him out of here.\"","Rachel nodded. \"Text me when the coast is clear.\"","She stepped into the hallway and nearly walked straight into Alpha Sebastian.","He was back already.","White shirt. Dark vest. Red roses in one hand and a CVS bag in the other.","He looked like the perfect husband.","Rachel knew he was full of it.","She lowered her head and tried to pass him.","\"Excuse me, miss.\"","Rachel stopped cold.","Inside the restroom, Eira froze with her hand on the door.","Alpha Sebastian’s gaze dropped to Rachel’s jacket.","\"Were you just in the fertility class?\""]},{"number":86,"title":"Chapter 86 Why Should I?","paragraphs":["\"Miss.\" Alpha Sebastian called out again.","Rachel took a breath and turned around, cool as she could manage.","\"Me?\"","\"Yeah.\" Alpha Sebastian walked over, smooth as ever, playing the perfect husband. \"Sorry to bother you, but could you run this in to my wife? She’s stuck in the restroom.\"","He held out a black plastic bag. Rachel clocked the drugstore logo instantly. Pads.","Good. He still had no clue.","She snatched the bag and went back inside.","\"Hey, your husband wanted me to give you this.\" Rachel said it loud enough for Alpha Sebastian to catch through the door.","Eira’s hand appeared under the stall. \"Thanks.\"","She ripped the wrapper open on purpose, used one, then walked out swinging the empty bag.","\"Eira.\" Alpha Sebastian’s face lit up like a kid on Christmas. He practically jogged over.","Roses. A whole bunch of them.","Last time he’d handed her flowers was their wedding day.","Eira clocked the hope written all over his face and took them anyway.","\"No purse?\" He eyed the plastic bag. She shook her head. He took it off her hands and grabbed the other one instead.","\"C’mon, let’s grab lunch.\"","\"Sure.\" She let him steer her toward a restaurant a few doors down. Not that she wanted to be there. She just went along for the ride.","Food hadn’t even hit the table yet when Alpha Sebastian sucked in a breath and finally manned up about Sterling House.","\"Eira, can you just let go of what Isabella did?\"","Eira’s glass stopped halfway to her mouth. Her voice came out flat.","\"So you finally know it was her.\"","\"Yeah.\" He nodded. \"I dropped the ball keeping her in check. My bad. I’m sorry.\"","\"And I’m sorry I made you go home and grovel to her that day.\"","He looked sincere enough. Didn’t matter anymore. Bottom line, he knew his sister pulled something messed up, and he was still riding for her. His wife could take a back seat.","\"You didn’t do anything.\" Eira kept her voice level. \"So why are you the one apologizing?\"","Sebastian didn’t answer right away.","\"Funny.\" A small, humorless smile touched her lips. \"Last I checked, she’s got a mouth of her own.\"","\"I’m apologizing on her behalf.\" His brow creased. \"And to you. Can we just drop it already?\"","Hearing that on repeat felt like getting jabbed with the same needle, over and over.","\"Why should I?\" Her voice sharpened.","\"If you forgive her, my parents will notice. She’ll notice. It’ll go a long way.\" Same old song. \"Keeps the family from falling apart. The Pack could use the stability right now.\"","Eira looked down and drained her water. Ice cold going down.","\"So all those years I hunted down the most renowned pack doctors in the region, tracked down rare herbs deep in contested territory, all just to ease the ache from your father’s old battle wounds, that counted for nothing.\"","\"Your mother almost lost her inheritance to a rogue posing as a Pack broker. I dug through his background for weeks, traced his real Pack ties, and got the Pack Council to shut him down. Also nothing.\"","\"Isabella picked a fight with a Beta from a rival Pack and it nearly started a border dispute. I was the one who smoothed it over with their Alpha, sat through three tense mediations, and made sure nobody’s territory got torched over her temper. None of that counted.\"","\"She drugged me. Almost got me assaulted. But if I forgive that, suddenly your family remembers I’m not so bad?\"","Alpha Sebastian’s eyes shrank. He had nothing.","\"That’s not,\" he started, wanting to say that’s not what I meant. Except every word out of her mouth checked out.","He shut up. Something ugly twisted in his chest.","Eira barely noticed anymore. Every time she butted heads with his family, he either told her to cave first or said absolutely nothing. The only time he actually kept quiet was when the Hales crossed a real line, and even then, knowing full well they were wrong, he never once had her back.","Staying neutral when the field wasn’t level? That was just picking a side without the guts to say so.","Eira stared at him without blinking.","Alpha Sebastian couldn’t meet her eyes.","Their food showed up, her grilled chicken and his steak. He picked up his fork, cut off a piece of steak, and set it on the edge of her plate before he said anything else.","\"You must be hungry. Eat something.\"","Old Eira would’ve backed off right here. She used to hate seeing Alpha Sebastian stuck in the middle, hated watching him look sad or torn up inside.","Not today. She ignored the guilt on his face and kept pushing.","\"Actually, I don’t think Isabella had the guts to pull this off alone.\"","Alpha Sebastian’s head snapped up. \"What do you mean?\"","\"Isabella only picks on people weaker than her. She’s a coward. That’s why she kept switching dorm rooms every time someone actually stood up to her. You know what that drug even is? The one she used on me?\"","His eyes shrank again.","\"That’s a federally controlled substance, Sebastian. Schedule I. You can’t grab that at a pharmacy, and you can’t order it online without leaving a trail a mile long. Isabella’s whole skill set is competing with other girls for attention. She barely knows how to run a coffee maker. You think she’s got some dealer on speed dial?\"","Serena, though? Serena had spent years overseas. Totally different story.","Eira looked at him closely. \"Has this ever crossed your mind? Isabella walked out of that police station clean. No charges. Not enough evidence, they said. That includes zero record of her buying anything, anywhere. Tracking’s crazy good these days. If she searched for it, ordered it, there’d be a paper trail somewhere. So why is there nothing?\"","Alpha Sebastian’s whole body locked up.","Because none of what Eira just said was wrong.","\"You always used to say someone talked Isabella into it. That she got played into doing something stupid. Honestly? I agreed with you. Isabella’s easy to manipulate.\"","\"You didn’t build what you built by drinking your way through business dinners, Sebastian. You’re smart. Use your head. Think it through.\"","Eira went back to her food, calm as ever.","Alpha Sebastian kept chewing, barely tasting anything. His mind kept circling back to that day at the hotel.","The only people involved besides Isabella were...","Serena.","No. No way.","Serena had always been sweet. She never once talked trash about Eira in front of him. That day at the hotel, she’d been the one calming him down, telling him maybe Isabella got confused, telling him not to lose it.","\"I’m done,\" Eira said.","\"Okay.\" Alpha Sebastian snapped out of it and asked, gentle, \"You want more water?\"","\"I got it.\" Eira took a sip, grabbed a napkin, wiped her mouth. \"I need to head back for the afternoon session. Don’t want to be late.\"","Alpha Sebastian stood up. He hesitated, then asked, \"Can you forgive us?\"","Forgiveness. All he wanted was to feel less guilty.","Eira didn’t answer that straight. Instead she said, \"If you want me to drop the complaint, Isabella apologizes to me herself. Face to face.\"","\"That’s it? Just an apology?\"","\"Yeah.\" Alpha Sebastian jumped on that fast. \"I’ll have her come apologize tomorrow.\"","\"Tomorrow doesn’t work.\" Eira shut that down. \"As for when, Isabella can wait until I let her know.\"","Alpha Sebastian frowned. \"Why?\"","\"Isabella made me wait when she stole my package,\" Eira said, flat.","His frown deepened. \"Eira, can’t you just take the high road here? Does everything have to be tit for tat?\""]},{"number":87,"title":"Chapter 87 The Divorce Papers Are Coming Through Fast","paragraphs":["\"If I’m dropping the charges, shouldn’t there be some payback?\" Eira shot back, calm as ever. \"Besides, I’m just making her wait a bit. I’ve got class this weekend. Unless you think I should skip it.\"","Alpha Sebastian sighed. \"Of course you should go. But once you quit and move back home, we can start trying for a baby.\"","\"Sure.\" Eira’s voice stayed flat. She turned and walked off, leaving the roses sitting on the chair.","Alpha Sebastian grabbed the flowers and chased after her, insisting on driving her to class himself. He shoved the roses back into her arms and pulled her into a hug, right there in front of everyone.","\"That’s Mrs. Hale, right? Her husband drove her here himself. They’re so sweet together.\"","\"Man, what a good husband. Spends money on his wife and brings her flowers too. Mine would never do anything that romantic. I had to beg for weeks just to sign up for this class.\"","Alpha Sebastian caught every word, and his mouth curved into a smug little smile. He soaked up every envious glance like sunlight.","He pulled Eira a little closer.","Her whole body went stiff. \"Class is starting.\"","\"Okay.\" Reluctance flickered in his eyes as he finally let her go.","With him still watching, Eira had no choice but to walk into the classroom. She grabbed a seat in the back corner, just like she and Rachel had planned. Keep it low-key.","Eira sat through the first half of class like a model student, eyes forward, spine straight, giving nothing away.","The moment she was sure Alpha Sebastian had left, the act dropped. She slipped out to the restroom and swapped clothes with Rachel again.","Rachel whispered, \"Okay, I’ll admit sneaking around like secret agents is kind of fun. But we can’t keep this up forever, right?\"","\"We won’t have to.\" Eira ran the numbers in her head. \"By next weekend, you won’t need to be careful at all.\"","\"Why not?\"","Because by then, the divorce will be final.","\"Never mind, forget I asked.\" Rachel rubbed her belly gently, her face soft. She was already pregnant.","Eira noticed. \"Congrats. I recorded the first half of class for you. You can catch up later.\"","\"You’re the best.\" Rachel pulled her mask up, let her hair fall forward to hide most of her face, and slipped back into the classroom.","--","Eira got back to Number Nine Southridge Estates around four.","Alpha Killian was already gone.","She walked into the dining room, sleeves rolled up, ready to bus the table like she always did back at the Hale place. Then she froze. The table gleamed. Tablecloth smooth, dead center, not a wrinkle in sight.","She actually looked around for a second, half expecting to find a stranger in the house.","Outside, the sky hung gray and heavy. A breeze slipped through the cracked window and flicked a note off the table.","She picked it up.","One word, written in Alpha Killian’s messy handwriting.","Kitchen.","She headed in and pushed the door open.","Spotless. Sink didn’t have a single crumb in it. A pair of pink and blue rubber gloves sat on the counter like they were on display. And there, a brand new dishwasher, sleek and white, practically screaming I cost more than your car.","She popped it open. Dishes inside sat clean, dry, still warm from the cycle.","Another note on top.","Fridge.","—Killian","Eira stood there a beat, taking in the whole spotless setup. Something warm and unfamiliar crept into her chest.","She opened the fridge. A few plates sat wrapped up inside, leftovers from lunch.","One more note.","You hate wasting food. Go eat it.","—Killian","She cracked a smile before she could stop herself.","He wasn’t wrong. She’d rather go hungry than toss out a single bite. Growing up in the Omega group home, wasting food just wasn’t a thing. Too many nights going to bed on an empty stomach to ever throw something away.","The Hales used to rip on her for it constantly. Called it trashy, said marrying in didn’t scrub the low-class off her.","Eira reheated the leftovers, sat down, and actually took her time eating. Savored it. Couldn’t remember the last time a meal alone felt this good.","She finished, plate wiped clean, and snapped a pic for her feed. Hales blocked, obviously.","Caption: Clean plate club.","Then she loaded her dishes into the new machine and fired off a text.","Eira: The dishwasher’s great, by the way. Thanks.","Killian: Sterling Group makes those.","Eira could practically hear the quiet pride behind that one line.","Eira: Impressive, Alpha Sterling.","His mouth twitched into a smirk.","Killian: Save the flattery.","--","Two days later, Alpha Sebastian swung by the Hale estate.","His parents were in the middle of a hushed conversation about the divorce papers when they heard the lock click. They shut up fast, voices dying mid-sentence.","Then the door opened and it was their son. Thank the Moon Goddess for sharp wolf hearing, or they’d have never caught themselves in time.","\"You’re back.\" Luna Margaret walked over. \"Serena said you’ve been swamped. You haven’t been answering her much.\"","Alpha Sebastian hung up his coat. His parents looked way too happy.","\"What’s going on? You two look like you won the lottery.\"","Of course we do. We’re about to get rid of that useless, jobless, barren daughter-in-law.","\"It’s a surprise.\" Luna Margaret kept it light, though she noticed the exhaustion on his face right away. \"We’ll tell you once it’s locked in. You look wiped out, sweetheart.\"","\"Work’s part of it.\" The other part was what Eira said to him. Her words kept looping in his head, wouldn’t let him rest.","He didn’t want to suspect Serena.","Maybe he should just talk to Isabella first.","\"Where’s Isabella?\" Just saying her name darkened his whole face.","Luna Margaret’s smile slipped. He was still stuck on that.","\"Siblings don’t hold grudges overnight, Alpha Sebastian. Don’t come at her with that face when she gets back. You’ll scare her half to death.\"","\"Where is she?\"","\"Serena took her shopping. That big procurement bid’s coming up, right? Serena wants a killer outfit for the signing ceremony.\" Luna Margaret’s excitement kept climbing. \"Once your company wins that contract, you’ll be repping Hale Group, she’ll be repping the federal project team. The press is gonna eat that up. Power couple of the year.\"","Especially since the divorce would be final before the bid even got announced. Luna Margaret was practically giddy over the timing.","Alpha Sebastian only caught one thing out of all that.","\"She screwed up and she’s out shopping?\" His voice dropped, sharp as a blade. \"She should be figuring out how to say sorry to Eira.\"","He pulled out his phone and called his sister. \"Wrap it up. Come home. We need to talk.\"","Alpha Roger set down his magazine, eyes on his son. \"You’re actually gonna make Isabella apologize to Eira?\"","\"She has to, if Eira’s dropping the charges.\" Alpha Sebastian caught the look on both their faces and sighed. \"Mom. Dad. Isabella messed up. She should say sorry. And it’s not just anyone she wronged, it’s Eira. Eira’s my Luna. She’s Luna to this whole Pack. Every wolf in Hale Pack owes her respect. That includes my own sister.\"","He paused, Eira’s voice cutting back through his head. Isabella barely knows how to run a coffee maker. You think she’s got a dealer on speed dial?","\"And there’s something else I need to ask her about.\""]},{"number":88,"title":"Chapter 88 Something Else","paragraphs":["Isabella’s stomach dropped, staring at her phone.","\"He yell at you?\" Serena caught the caller ID.","\"No. Just told me to get home. But I can tell he’s fuming.\" Isabella fired off a text to her mom. The reply came fast. Her eyes went wide. \"He wants me to apologize to Eira? Seriously?\"","Serena’s eyes snagged on the line underneath.","[ Something else. Sebastian had something bigger he needed to ask.]","Her gut clenched. Had to be about Eira. Which meant it was about that day at the Sterling House.","Alpha Sebastian had been drifting closer to Eira lately, further from her by the day.","\"Don’t sweat it.\" Serena stroked Isabella’s hair, sweet as pie. \"Bet Eira’s whispering in his ear again.\"","\"Right? This is all on her.\" Isabella pouted, easy to play as ever. \"Sebastian’s been riding me hard, always taking her side now.\"","\"Come home with me. Maybe I can talk him down.\"","\"I don’t know.\" Serena hesitated, playing it up. \"Things with Sebastian are rocky right now.\"","Isabella melted with sympathy. \"Don’t stress. Nobody likes Eira. He’s into you, just too stubborn to admit it. He’s only still with her out of guilt.\"","Disgust flickered and vanished across Serena’s face. Alpha Roger and Alpha Sebastian were the only Hales worth two cents. Luna Margaret and Isabella, cut from the same cheap cloth.","\"I’m actually scared,\" Serena said, careful with every word. \"What if he thinks I was in on it? You’re his sister, he’ll yell and move on. Me? I don’t get that pass. He finds out, he’s done with me. Straight back to Eira.\"","Serena’s aim landed dead on.","\"Relax. I’m not dumb. None of this touches you. Mom and Dad don’t care. He’s just pitching a fit.\"","\"You’re the best.\" Serena stroked her hair again, same energy as petting a dog that just did a trick.","The two of them showed up at the Hale estate together.","\"Feels like it’s been forever,\" Serena said, all smiles.","\"Work’s been crazy.\" Alpha Sebastian’s face twisted, watching that warm smile.","He poured Serena a glass of water, parked her in the living room. Isabella, his study, now. Alone.","Door clicked shut. Soundproof. Nothing getting out.","Alpha Sebastian cut straight to it. \"Sterling House. Who else was in on it?\"","\"Just me. Who else would there even be?\" Isabella rolled her eyes. \"Come on, Sebastian, quit giving me so much credit.\"","Watching her act this smug about it lit Alpha Sebastian up.","\"Watch your mouth. You screwed up bad, and you’re gonna get sassy with me?\"","\"Eira’s fine, isn’t she?\" Isabella waved it off.","\"And if she wasn’t?\" Alpha Sebastian snapped, chest tightening at just the thought.","\"Cut the act. Somebody help you? Don’t make me find out myself, or it’s not just your cards getting frozen.\"","\"Go ahead, freeze ’em.\" Isabella shot back.","She had Serena now. Forget stingy Eira, Serena actually spent money.","\"It was all me. Nobody else. I already did a night in a holding cell, what more do you want?\" She whined it out, playing victim hard.","Alpha Sebastian wasn’t having it. \"Where’d the drug come from? Who’s your guy?\"","\"I... found it online.\"","\"Buy it online, feds trace that in a heartbeat.\" His glare cut sharp. \"Isabella. That’s trafficking. Federal charge. Long as Eira doesn’t drop this, it stays open, and eventually they find your source. Can’t wait to see who’s covering for you then.\"","Isabella’s eyes went wide. Actually rattled now.","\"It’s not that deep. I’ll apologize to Eira. Done.\"","\"You’re apologizing either way.\" Alpha Sebastian exhaled slow. \"But you’re also telling me who hooked you up.\"","\"Hooked me up with what? Quit talking like this is some cartel thing.\" Her hands started shaking.","Alpha Sebastian read her face close.","Isabella was a coward, always had been. No shot she pulled this off solo.","\"Who helped you. Was it...\" Serena’s name sat right on his tongue. He bit it back.","Fist clenched at his side.","\"I... I...\" Isabella’s brain spun.","[Sebastian finds out Serena’s involved, he’s done with her for good. And Eira’s stuck in this house forever.]","That thought stiffened her spine right back up.","\"I just ran into some guy. He had it, I bought it.\" She dug in, playing martyr in her own head, doing it all for the family, for Alpha Sebastian and Serena.","This is all Eira’s fault. She just won’t drop it.","\"Did Eira say something to you? She thinks I did this with Serena, doesn’t she? She’s trying to drag Serena down with me!\" Isabella’s voice climbed. \"What kind of woman goes after her husband’s friends like that? You know Serena, Sebastian. Why are you buying whatever Eira’s selling?\"","\"She’s jealous, plain and simple. Can’t stand you having female friends, wants you all to herself. It’s sad, honestly.\"","Alpha Sebastian’s face shifted. \"You think Eira’s jealous?\"","\"Duh.\" Isabella rolled her eyes. \"Eira’s not exactly a saint, Sebastian. You can’t just swallow everything she says.\"","\"Serena’s been grinding overseas for years, and every spare second, she’s thinking about you. She finds out you suspected her? She’s gonna be gutted. I’m telling her right now.\"","Isabella made a show of storming for the door.","\"Stop.\" Alpha Sebastian’s voice went flat and hard. He stepped in front of her, blocking her out. \"So you’re telling me this was all you. Solo mission.\"","\"I’m done talking to you. I’m telling Serena you don’t trust her.\" Isabella wrenched the door open. Alpha Sebastian caught her arm before she cleared it.","\"Fine. We’re done here.\" He let it drop, chose to believe his sister. And Serena, apparently.","\"But you’re apologizing to Eira. She’s not dropping the charges till you do.\" Alpha Sebastian held her gaze. \"And if this drags on, word gets out. Every Pack within a hundred miles hears a Hale drugged her own Luna. No Alpha out there’s putting a mark on someone tangled up in an investigation like that. You can kiss every offer you got this year goodbye.\"","Isabella’s eyes went wide. \"I’ll say sorry right now!\"","Sorry cost her nothing. Never had.","\"You made her wait when you swiped her stuff. Now it’s your turn to wait.\"","\"Is she out of her mind?\" Isabella’s temper flared. \"What if this wrecks every offer I’ve got lined up?\"","Alpha Sebastian just shook his head and walked out ahead of her.","--","Hearing the door open, Serena stood, eyes cutting straight to Isabella.","Isabella flashed her a shaky thumbs-up.","Serena dropped her gaze fast, burying the flicker of satisfaction underneath. Then she walked over. \"You didn’t go too hard on her, did you?\"","\"He totally did!\" Isabella whined, glomming onto Serena’s arm. \"I already said I’d apologize. He still chewed me out.\"","\"Sebastian, she knows she screwed up. Cut her some slack?\" Serena’s eyes went wide, all innocence.","Alpha Sebastian stared into that clean, guileless face. How’d he ever doubt her?","But he couldn’t exactly blame Eira either.","Eira was jealous.","Jealous.","The word landed in his chest, and weirdly, it didn’t sting. It felt kind of good.","Eira cares.","\"Sebastian? You zone out on me?\"","\"Nah, I’m good.\" He shook it off.","Serena caught the dodge anyway. Stung more than she let on.","Her phone buzzed right then.","[Hi, this is the Office of Sponsored Research, just a courtesy call. Your grant account got flagged yesterday for a compliance review, part of a larger audit into one of your funding sources. Formal documentation’s already on its way to your inbox, wanted to give you a heads-up before it lands.]","Serena’s brow furrowed.","She’d never requested any review.","Never asked anyone to look into anything."]},{"number":89,"title":"Chapter 89 Caught in the Act","paragraphs":["Serena Winthrop was never poor. Old Pack money, connections most people only dream about.","But research ate cash like nothing else. Millions, nonstop, for gear, staff, the works.","Her grandfather backed her, guided her, but even he couldn’t just siphon family funds into some long-shot project. The Winthrop Pack had obligations. That money belonged to a hundred people, not just one granddaughter chasing a dream.","That’s when she clocked Alpha Sebastian Hale’s rise. And that’s when she made her move.","Alpha Sebastian still loved her. One ask, and the money started flowing. Three hundred grand, every month, like clockwork. That kind of cash made her overseas gig a total breeze. Gear, materials, whatever she needed, covered.","Her own family could’ve paid for it too. Money was never the problem. The issue was every dollar came with strings, approvals, the whole Pack’s interests riding on it.","Alpha Sebastian’s money hit different. Fast. No questions. No paperwork trail leading back to a boardroom full of relatives.","Which made it a ticking time bomb.","Somebody digs into where that money’s really coming from, she’s cooked. And Alpha Sebastian’s married. Eira finds out he’s been quietly funding another woman’s career and decides to go after it in the divorce? Serena’s whole world implodes.","She already had her cover story locked and loaded. Private investment. Business call. Nothing more.","Except she never asked for any expense report.","Her inbox sat empty.","Serena stood there, scrolling like a maniac. Nothing. No request, no email, nothing.","\"Sebastian!\"","She crossed the room, voice cracking. \"Someone’s been impersonating me. Called the institute overseas, wanted a full breakdown of every dollar you’ve—\"","She caught herself.","Still Hale Pack land. Wolf ears caught whispers through closed doors, and this wasn’t a secret built to survive one.","Pack money, quietly funding his ex’s lab overseas. One wolf hears it, the whole Pack hears it by morning.","And they wouldn’t be asking about a grant. They’d be asking what kind of Alpha spends Pack funds on his ex, and what else he’s been hiding.","Alpha Sebastian’s jaw tightened. He’d caught it too.","He said nothing. Just grabbed her hand and pulled her straight for the door, out past the walls, where the wind ate words before wolf ears ever got the chance.","Once they cleared the walls, Serena laid it all out, face tight with worry. \"Sebastian, does Eira know about the money?\"","He shook his head, studying her. \"You think it was Eira?\"","\"No.\" Shut down instantly.","Eira wouldn’t know where to even look. She never touched the accounts, never asked a single question about his money. Come to think of it, she was a rock-solid wife. Never complained, never dug for dirt.","Ethan’s voice popped into his head. \"Dude, your wife’s a machine. Runs the house, handles your parents, handles your sister, never once complains. How are you not whipped for her?\"","Whipped.","His mind wandered somewhere he didn’t expect.","Serena clocked the shift in his face instantly. Jealousy flared hot.","\"You trust her that much?\"","He snapped back. \"It’s not her. Maybe this is just some routine flag, could be totally random.\"","\"Random?\" She stared him down. \"Sebastian, you don’t believe me.\"","\"I do. If I didn’t, I’d have suspected you the second Isabella pulled that stunt.\"","Serena froze. \"What’s that got to do with me?\" Voice sharp now. \"Why would you even go there?\"","A woman’s tears hit harder than any argument. Her eyes went glassy, and Alpha Sebastian knew instantly he’d screwed up.","\"I’m not accusing you of anything.\"","\"You are.\" Her voice cracked. \"Isabella can’t keep a secret to save her life. If I was in on it, she’d have spilled same day. So it was Eira. She said something, didn’t she?\"","He didn’t answer fast enough.","Serena wiped a tear, smile turning bitter. \"Right. You’re married. She talks, you listen. She points at me, you follow. Years, Sebastian. Guess that’s nothing next to four years with her.\"","\"Let’s just call us a one-time thing. Pretend none of this ever mattered.\" She turned to walk.","She knew better. No way a guy loyal to her this long just lets her walk.","\"Serena!\"","Called it.","He grabbed her hand. She yanked away first try. Softer the second. Let him keep it the third.","She stopped, turned, eyes wet. \"Kiss me. Kiss me and I’ll believe you.\"","He looked at her lips. Eira’s face flashed through his head instead.","He froze up.","Serena went for it first, up on her toes, arms around his neck, deepening it. When he still wasn’t into it, she pulled her ace card.","\"I love you, Sebastian. I love you so much.\"","Same three words worked at his apartment that night too, the ones that had him pulling her in, fumbling with her dress, drunk on more than just liquor. Same three words worked at the gala, whispered against his ear with her teeth grazing his lobe, and his hands were all over her within seconds.","Worked again.","His hands landed on her waist.","There it is. Her smile turned smug. Men never stood a chance against her, especially not a guy who’d carried a torch for her this long.","\"Sebastian... Sebastian...\" She was melting into it when a shove yanked her back hard.","His hands. Pushing her off.","\"Sebastian?\" She blinked, thrown.","His eyes slid away. \"We’re in public. Cut it out.\"","Oh. That’s all.","Relief washed over her, and she turned the puppy eyes right back on. \"Then let’s head to the apartment. You haven’t swung by in over a week.\"","The penthouse he bought her.","\"Let’s get you home.\" He started walking.","Serena caught up fast, arm looping through his, smile back in full force.","--","In the shadows of a nearby grove, a woman in a black hoodie lowered her camera and popped off the telephoto lens, sliding it into her backpack. She pulled the memory card, slotted it into a reader, and plugged it into her phone.","The photos loaded one by one.","Dozens of shots. Alpha Sebastian and Serena holding hands. Wrapped up in each other. Kissing.","Each file ran thirty, fifty megabytes easy. Crystal clear. Zoom in tight enough, you could count the pores on their skin."]},{"number":90,"title":"Chapter 90 The Cooling-Off Period Ends","paragraphs":["Miles got the high-res photos fast. He checked the details, then headed for Alpha Killian’s office with his tablet in hand.","\"Alpha Killian, the metadata’s got Serena living at The Celestia Residences downtown.\"","The Celestia Residences. A Sterling property.","\"Pulled the records too. She just bought a luxury penthouse there. Credit card on file for the purchase is under the name Hale.\"","Didn’t take a genius to figure out who that was. Alpha Sebastian.","Alpha Killian swiped through the photos one by one, disgust flickering across his face.","\"Keep all of these. We’ll need them later.\" He shoved the tablet back at Miles, done looking.","\"You confirmed the transfers? Three hundred grand a month, Alpha Sebastian to Serena?\"","\"Confirmed.\" Miles gave a faint smile. \"It’s all compiled.\"","\"Add the photos to the file.\"","\"Got it.\" Miles already knew exactly where this was heading. A small smile tugged at his mouth. Perfect ammo to take down a business rival.","\"Send a copy to Miss Crawford too.\" A promise was a promise. Eira wanted proof of every dollar.","\"Not the photos, though. I don’t want her eyes anywhere near that trash.\"","\"Understood.\"","Since her name was already on the table, Miles kept going. \"Her resignation still needs sign-off. HR’s waiting to close out her attendance, and accounting’s breathing down my neck too.\"","Alpha Killian’s brow creased. \"Already?\"","\"Next Wednesday’s her last day. Just handover and packing up her desk. Gotta kill her badge access too.\"","\"Fine.\" Short nod.","Miles walked out, pulled up the assistant group chat, fired off a message.","Miles: Talked to Alpha Killian. Unless something blows up, he’s signing off Monday.","Eira: Thanks, Miles.","Natalie: Wait, you’re actually bailing on us?? It’s gonna be just me and Kate again. Rude.","Eira: Still gonna be around Palo Alto. We’ll grab drinks whenever.","Kate: Got a plan lined up after this?","Eira: Some personal stuff first, then actual work.","Kate: Say the word, I’ll shoot you some job leads.","Eira: Appreciate it, but I’m good for now.","Natalie: Okay forget the sappy stuff. Before you go, you’re making one last batch of that banana bread, right? Non-negotiable. The whole floor’s been asking.","Kate: Seconding this. I will actually cry if it’s gone for good.","Miles: Same, honestly. That spicy stuff got me through Q3.","Eira laughed and typed back: Fine, fine. One last batch.","--","The next day, Eira called Miss Gwen and caught up for over an hour before bringing up the snacks.","Miss Gwen’s voice went warm the second she heard coworkers were paying money for them.","Made her happy on two fronts. Eira making friends at a real job, and her pups picking up some pocket cash of their own.","Half the pups in that shelter were orphaned wolves with no Pack backing them, no name to lean on, nobody sending money their way.","A little extra cash from baking meant something.","Alpha Sebastian didn’t try picking her up again that weekend. Just asked when she’d see Isabella.","She said a couple days. He didn’t push, just admitted he’d been slammed and knew he’d been slacking on her.","Eira shrugged it off. Texted back: All good. Work first.","Sunday was quiet. Eira spent the whole day at home, unwinding, no plans, no errands, just resting.","Monday morning, she was up before her alarm. Chopped vegetables, cooked up the beef and shrimp, scrambled a batch of eggs, cooked the rice.","Rolled everything into tortillas, wrapped them tight in foil while they were still warm, bagged them up plain. Six bags total.","Clocked in right after, ran into Vanessa in the lobby, handed her a bag.","Vanessa’s face lit up, then dropped. \"You’re really out soon, huh? Saw it this morning. Alpha Killian signed off.\"","Didn’t even make it a full month, after all that talk about keeping her on.","\"Guess my breakfast hookup’s drying up.\" Vanessa sighed, only half joking.","Eira smiled, said her goodbyes, walked in right on time, not early, not late.","She passed out the bags, one each.","Kate ditched her coffee on the spot, bummed a carton of milk off Natalie, and the three of them huddled together, unwrapping foil and digging in like it was the best thing that happened to them all week.","Window was cracked. Smell wasn’t loud, but it carried down the hall. Alpha Killian and Miles caught it walking in.","Alpha Killian’s steps slowed. His eyes cut toward the three of them.","Miles eyed the burritos, stomach already growling.","\"Miles.\" Eira held a bag out to him.","He wanted it bad, but with Alpha Killian standing right there, he wasn’t about to reach for it.","\"Hands broken?\" Alpha Killian’s voice came flat and sharp. \"Need her to hold it for you all morning?\"","Miles snatched it fast, already unwrapping the foil.","One bag left in Eira’s hand. Alpha Killian’s eyes tracked straight to it.","Miles caught the look and figured Alpha Killian was about to walk off without taking his share. Score. That meant one more burrito was up for grabs, and Miles already had his eye on it.","Eira turned to Alpha Killian. \"Breakfast?\"","\"No.\" Cold, flat. He walked straight past her.","She set the last bag down on her desk. \"Guess it’s mine, then.\"","Alpha Killian stopped mid-step.","Miles jumped in fast. \"She made one for you too, Alpha Killian. That’s the one right there.\"","Alpha Killian turned back, eyeing her sideways. Last time, the biscuits, nothing for him. Time before that, the snacks, nothing either. Now suddenly there’s a burrito with his name on it?","Kate caught on quick, grabbed the bag off Eira’s desk, and pressed it straight into Eira’s hands.","\"Breakfast.\" Eira held it out to him.","Miles moved to intercept, figuring Alpha Killian wouldn’t take food straight from her hand in front of everyone. Alpha Killian beat him to it, snatching the bag fast, shooting him a look on the way past.","He walked into his office, sat down, and cleared the whole thing without stopping.","Then he asked for next week’s schedule.","The week had barely even started.","Alpha privileges, apparently.","Eira pulled up the calendar and double-checked everything. Big item on next week’s list: the major bidding competition. She flagged it right at the top, impossible to miss.","As the bidding date crept closer, Alpha Killian’s Mondays turned into back-to-back meetings, nonstop.","Beyond the high-level Sterling Group sessions, he had to sit through meetings for each of the sixteen subsidiaries under the Sterling name.","Even with everything compressed and rushed, his Mondays and Tuesdays were eaten alive.","Everyone else clocked out at five. He stayed late, buried in overtime. Alpha Killian was slammed.","Alpha Sebastian was just as slammed.","Only Eira caught a break. She clocked in, clocked out, right on schedule, nobody bothering her.","Wednesday morning, Alpha Sebastian found a gap to call. \"Today’s your last day at Sterling, right?\"","\"Yeah.\" Eira glanced down at the handover checklist in her hand. \"Heading to the front desk now to close out my attendance records.\"","\"Good. I’ve been buried the past couple weeks, but once things calm down, let’s go out, celebrate a little.\"","His voice softened, noticeably.","\"Sounds good.\" Eira’s tone came out warm.","She sounded happy about it.","Just not for the reason he thought. The month she’d been waiting out was finally up."]},{"number":91,"title":"Chapter 91 I’ll Pick It Up Myself","paragraphs":["Eira ended the call.","The receptionist pulled up her file, confirmed payroll had nothing outstanding. No unpaid PTO, no reimbursements sitting in limbo.","Eira had never filed an expense report the whole time she worked there anyway, so that part took all of thirty seconds.","Handover dragged on for hours.","Kate was running point. They sat together going through the offboarding doc Eira had put together, access badges, laptop, anything tagged as company property.","Eira barely had anything to hand back. No laptop bag full of gadgets, no company car keys, nothing. She slid her badge across the table, and that was pretty much it.","Kate glanced at the desk, then back at her, brow raised. \"That’s it? Nothing else?\"","\"That’s it.\" Eira shrugged. \"Never really brought much in.\"","Kate scanned the desk again, empty, bare, not even a plant or a mug with some corny slogan on it. \"Girl, I’ve seen interns with more stuff on their desk than you. How do you even function in here?\"","\"Don’t need much to get through the day.\" Eira had planned this exit since day one. Only personal item she’d ever kept around was a water bottle, long gone now, already packed. Everything else on this desk belonged to the company, and she made sure it stayed that way.","Kate shook her head, half impressed, half done. \"No wonder your corner looked like a ghost town.\"","Doc wrapped, laptop closed. \"That’s everything on my end. Go find Alpha Killian, need his final sign-off before Vanessa can close your file.\"","Eira glanced toward his office. Phone glued to his ear, deep in some call. Couldn’t catch a word, but when he turned, she caught that sharp profile dead on.","Waited him out. Walked over. Knocked.","\"Come in.\" He set the phone down, stood by the window, one hand in his pocket, watching her walk in.","Hair pinned up with a pencil today, loose strands framing her face, same rimless glasses, same understated look, white blouse, dark jeans. Five-eight, lean, but there was something unbendable about the way she carried herself. No makeup, and her eyes still cut through the room anyway.","\"Just need your sign-off on the final paperwork. Should be sitting in your queue.\" She stopped a few feet from his desk.","His eyes lingered on her a beat too long before he walked over to his computer, pulled it up, clicked approve without blinking. Same speed as Monday’s resignation approval.","\"Done.\" He glanced back at her. \"Vanessa Cole’s got the rest. Only one cleared to close out your exit. Go find her.\"","\"Got it.\" She turned to go.","\"Hold on.\"","She stopped, looked back. \"Alpha Killian?\"","\"You got tight with Miles, Kate, Natalie.\" Even tone. \"You need a real send-off. Tomorrow, seven thirty, Eden Garden. Already got the reservation.\"","She wasn’t great at this part. Paused, then nodded, actually thrown. \"Thanks.\"","\"Mm.\" She turned to go again. One step out, stopped, turned back. \"Alpha Killian.\"","\"Yeah?\"","She hesitated, then looked him dead in the eye. \"That chip project you’re bidding on, the Sovereign Processor thing. Dig into why the government’s pushing so hard on it. There’s more going on than what’s on paper.\"","Beat.","\"Hope it works out for you.\"","Didn’t wait for a reply. Walked out, shut the door behind her.","She hadn’t planned on saying any of that. Just slipped out anyway.","She figured Alpha Killian was sharp enough to connect the dots himself. Whether Sterling actually landed the deal came down to what the company brought to the table, and whatever call the research institute made in the end.","His eyes stayed on the door long after she’d gone.","--","Vanessa had her paperwork ready in HR. Badge killed, system access pulled, credentials wiped. Fifteen minutes, done.","\"Keep the badge.\" She waved off Eira’s hand. \"And hey, you ever need a way back in somewhere, I’ve got contacts. Just say the word.\"","\"I’m good, but thanks.\"","\"Your loss.\" Vanessa grinned, swapped numbers with her anyway. \"See you around, Crawford.\"","Eira cleared her desk fast. Wiped the laptop, straightened everything, gone in five minutes flat. Kate and Natalie caught her on the way out, quick hugs, a reminder about Eden Garden tomorrow at seven thirty.","\"Don’t you dare bail,\" Kate called after her.","\"See you tomorrow night,\" Eira said instead of goodbye.","Outside, the air had gone cold. Her phone buzzed before she hit the sidewalk.","Sebastian.","\"All done?\"","\"Yeah.\"","\"Good. I’m crashing at the office tonight, don’t wait up. Get some sleep, skip breakfast tomorrow.\" A pause. \"Once the bid wraps up, I’ll get you something. Name it.\"","\"You already gave me what I wanted.\"","Silence on his end.","His chest went warm. She really does love me. Every time he asked, it was always something like that.","He smiled to himself. \"Nothing you want, huh? Guess I’ll surprise you, then.\"","She didn’t answer. Flagged a car, gave the driver an address low under her breath. \"Southridge Estates, Number Nine.\"","He hung up, turned to his assistant before the screen even went dark. \"Sign Eira up for driving lessons. And get her a car, nothing flashy, something practical. A sedan, decent trunk space for groceries and stuff.\"","In the back seat, Eira was already dialing someone else.","Two rings. Pickup.","\"Alpha Roger.\" She skipped the small talk. \"The Mate Status Dissolution Certificate came in already, right?\"","A beat of silence.","\"It’s here.\"","\"And the mate registry the Hale family’s been sitting on, all pulled together?\"","\"All set.\" Alpha Roger’s tone stayed flat, even. \"I can have someone run it over.\"","\"No need.\" She glanced out the window, city lights sliding past, voice dropping low. \"I’ll pick it up myself.\""]},{"number":92,"title":"Chapter 92 Free and Clear","paragraphs":["The Hale Estate.","Eira hadn’t been back in weeks. This place had swallowed years of her pain. Now she was walking out for good.","One breath. Doorbell.","Luna Margaret answered, oddly chipper. No small talk, straight to the study.","Alpha Roger pulled a black folder from his desk.","Four documents inside. Two Registered Mate Bond certificates. Two Mate Bond Dissolution certificates.","Eira’s eyes locked onto them. Her breathing slowed.","She reached out for them.","Alpha Roger’s hand landed on the folder first, holding it shut. His gaze went hard, something low and rough running under his words. \"You remember what you promised me?\"","\"I do.\" Eira dragged her eyes off the certificates and met his stare head-on. \"I won’t go around broadcasting it. Somebody doesn’t know Sebastian and I were together, I’m not bringing it up. Somebody already knows, I won’t be the one telling them we’re done.\"","Luna Margaret stepped up beside her husband, eyes drilling into Eira. \"Swear you won’t wreck my son’s future. Swear you won’t breathe a word about him and Serena to anybody.\"","Eira said nothing at first. Just looked between the two of them.","\"I won’t bring it up first.\"","But if somebody asked her straight out, that was a different story.","Luna Margaret caught the loophole instantly. \"Swear you won’t tell anyone. Period.\"","Before those certificates showed up, Eira barely flinched at their threats. Now that they were sitting right there in that folder, she cared even less.","\"Can’t promise that.\" Her voice stayed steady. \"My mentor’s widow. The woman who raised me at the shelter. The people who actually give a damn about me. They deserve the truth. I’ve got no reason to hide it from them.\"","Fair point. Luna Margaret had nothing to throw back.","Alpha Roger’s knuckles paled against the folder. \"Watch your tone.\" His voice dropped, carrying that particular weight only an Alpha’s voice could pull off, the kind that made lesser wolves want to bare their throats without thinking. \"You forget who you’re talking to.\"","Eira didn’t flinch. She’d stopped flinching a long time ago.","Alpha Roger exhaled, reeling it back in. \"Fine. Tell whoever you want in your own circle. But you don’t tell Sebastian. Not yet. He’s in the middle of the biggest deal of his career. You don’t get to blow that up for him.\"","\"You can’t agree to that, these don’t leave this room.\"","Alpha Roger’s hand hovered over the folder, ready to lock it back in the drawer.","Eira’s fingers curled slightly. She knew freedom was sitting right in front of her. She just had to play along a little longer.","\"Deal.\"","Alpha Roger paused.","\"I won’t tell Sebastian we’re done until the Sovereign Processor bid wraps up.\" She held out her hand.","Alpha Roger’s face stayed carved from stone. \"Out of respect for the years you looked after my son, I’ll trust you on this one.\"","Eira took her two certificates and stepped back.","She opened the registration certificate first.","Right in the center, both their names.","Registered Mate Bond: Sebastian Hale & Eira Crawford.","Below that, the date, the family name, the bond registry number. She remembered that day clear as anything. Standing in the middle of a crowd, smiling, actually believing she’d belong to this family, this Pack, forever. Her fingers brushed lightly over the photo.","Then she flipped to the next one.","A silver seal caught the light.","Mate Bond Dissolution Certificate.","Cold, flat text underneath.","The mate bond between Sebastian Hale and Eira Crawford has been dissolved.","Two stamps sat beside the photo, the Hale family crest and the official werewolf registry seal, both pressed hard into the paper.","Her lips twitched. She nearly laughed. Caught herself before it showed, tucked it back down, kept her eyes on the paper instead.","To Alpha Roger and Luna Margaret, watching her go quiet like that, it read as her barely holding it together. Putting on a brave face.","Luna Margaret’s laugh came out cold, satisfied.","No Pack behind her now. No Alpha backing her up. Luna Margaret figured she’d find out fast just how little a wolf was worth out there without a Pack.","Best case, some rich old wolf’s second mate down the road. Raising someone else’s pups.","Luna Margaret could already see the whole washed-up future. Didn’t even bother hiding the smugness.","See? Cut loose from the name, cut loose from her son, cut loose from any Pack at all. Eira Crawford was nothing.","\"Got what you came for.\" Luna Margaret’s voice turned gleeful. \"Door’s that way.\"","Eira only took her own copies.","\"Don’t forget Sebastian’s set,\" she said, flat. \"He’ll need the dissolution paperwork if he’s marrying Serena.\"","Alpha Roger’s jaw tightened. \"Don’t need you telling us how to run this family. He’ll get them when it’s time.\"","\"Good.\" She held the papers tight, turned for the door.","Walked out without looking back.","--","Isabella came through the door with her arms full of shopping bags, some influencer-approved boutique haul probably, and froze the second she clocked Eira standing there. Her whole face soured on the spot.","\"What the hell are you doing in my house? Snooping around the study, huh? What’d you take?\"","Classic. Not the first time she’d tried this garbage.","Back when Eira first married in the family, Isabella tried the same move at Sunday dinner. Stormed in late, dropped into her chair, announced to the table like breaking news, \"Somebody’s been using my face cream. Who touched it?\"","Eyes locked on Eira the whole time.","Made zero sense. Every suite in that house had its own bathroom, Isabella’s included.","Eira had never once set foot inside Isabella’s room, let alone her bathroom.","But logic never mattered when Isabella wanted a target, and nobody in that house ever bothered calling her out on it.","Years later, Isabella was still slinging accusations around like they cost her nothing.","Eira’s face went stone cold. \"Keep running that mouth, I’ll shut it for you.\"","\"You—\" Isabella’s eyes went huge.","Eira gave her a small, tight smile. \"Don’t worry about it.\"","Isabella’s face went red as a fire truck, but right before she could really lose it, Alpha Roger and Luna Margaret walked out of the study.","She froze mid-breath.","\"Dad? Mom?\" Bags hit the couch. \"Why is she here?\"","\"Business.\" Luna Margaret brushed it off like it was nothing.","Isabella scoffed. \"What kind of business could you possibly have with her? She walks in, the whole place smells like a dumpster.\"","\"Funny, I think that every time you’re home.\" Eira kept her voice flat, bored almost.","Isabella’s face went full tomato.","Luna Margaret grabbed her daughter’s arm, shot Eira a look sharp enough to cut glass. \"You’re not welcome here. Get out.\"","Isabella lifted her chin, feeling brave now that mom had her back. \"You heard her. Hit the road.\"","Eira’s eyes landed on Isabella, and a slow smile spread across her face.","\"Isabella. Tomorrow night, ten sharp. Room 9908, The Sterling House. Show up, say you’re sorry, and I’ll let this whole thing go.\"","The smugness drained right out of Isabella’s face. Her stomach dropped like she’d missed a step going downstairs.","Same time, same place. Is she about to pull that again?","\"Dad... Mom...\"","Eira was already pulling the door shut behind her when she caught the shake creeping into Isabella’s voice."]},{"number":93,"title":"Chapter 93 Breaking Point","paragraphs":["After she left the Hale Estate, Eira skipped going home.","She Ubered to a little Italian spot she’d never been to, the kind of place with checkered tablecloths and candles stuck in old wine bottles. Nothing about it screamed the Hales. That was the whole appeal.","She ordered whatever she wanted for once. Truffle pasta, a glass of Chianti, tiramisu for dessert. No rush. No one to report back to.","Her own private little party of one.","Back home, she showered, threw on an old T-shirt, and set the dissolution certificate on her nightstand like a trophy. Lights off. Lay down.","The apartment was dead quiet. Quiet enough she could hear herself breathing.","She closed her eyes. Waited for sleep.","Didn’t happen.","Her brain wouldn’t shut up. Old memories kept looping, tangled up with her to-do list for tomorrow.","Sebastian. Her ex now. Just like that. Done was done, nothing left to chew on there.","Tomorrow had better things on it. Gifts for Kate, Natalie, and Miles topped the list.","Kate was a no-brainer, gift card to Sephora, maybe a cute pair of heels.","Natalie was easy too, anything from the candy aisle plus one of those oversized stuffed animals from Target.","Miles was the wild card. She’d never clocked what he was into, but the guy swapped glasses like other people swapped outfits. A glasses chain, maybe. Something a little ironic.","Then there was Alpha Killian.","What do you even get a guy who already owns everything?","She had zero game when it came to buying gifts for men. Her only frame of reference was Sebastian, and that track record was garbage.","Dress shirts. Oxfords. Ties, cufflinks. Toothbrush, razor, the whole nine yards. Stuff she used to grab off his Amazon wishlist without a second thought.","Sebastian, again. Her eyes popped open. Nope. Not doing this tonight.","She grabbed her phone, thumbed open Google.","Good gift ideas for your Boss.","Turns out there’s a whole etiquette to it. Go too big and it looks like a bribe. Go too cheap and it looks like you don’t respect the guy. Half the results pushed some regional snack box thing.","Hard pass. She barely had any of that left over for herself.","She almost gave up, then thought about the last two weeks. Alpha Killian running on maybe four hours of sleep, that burnt vending machine coffee he kept grabbing between meetings because he never had time to leave the building.","Something clicked.","She typed in a new search. Best coffee gift for someone who works too much.","That one landed. Roaster reviews, a Reddit thread on portable espresso makers, one YouTube guy ranking desk gear, and she was out cold before she made it through the third video.","Her internal clock beat the alarm again, like always. Sunlight was already sneaking through the blinds.","Eira spent the morning on the porch, catching some rays, no plans, no rush, just soaking up a little vitamin D.","Afternoon rolled around and she hit the mall.","Gift list was already locked in from the night before: makeup for Kate, a stuffed animal for Natalie, a glasses chain for Miles, coffee gear for Alpha Killian.","Kate and Natalie’s gifts took ten minutes each, in and out. Miles took a bit longer. She got stuck deciding between two chains and just said screw it, bought both.","Alpha Killian’s gift came last. She found a specialty coffee shop and picked up a bag of some fancy single-origin roast, plus a compact espresso maker small enough to toss in a backpack.","Gifts, done. Round two: retail therapy.","She used to budget like her life depended on it, half her paycheck on bills, half on the shelter.","Sebastian ate well, dressed sharp, she made sure of that every single time. None of that was her problem anymore. She swiped her card without even glancing at the total, once.","DSW, Sephora, some boutique she’d walked past a hundred times and never once gone into. Bags piled up fast.","Somewhere between stores, she called Miss Gwen for updated height and weight numbers on the shelter kids.","Winter was coming, and those coats weren’t going to order themselves.","Back home, Eira hung everything up, lined her new shoes by the door, then hit a wall. Zero clue how to put any of it together. Lila texted right on cue, so they hopped on FaceTime.","\"Point the camera at your closet,\" Lila said.","\"That white wool coat, the turtleneck, the wide-leg pants. Now shoes...\"","\"White sneakers?\" Eira swung the camera toward a pair of white flats. \"Bag too, right?\"","\"Now you’re speaking my language.\" Lila grinned, then groaned. \"Okay, gotta bounce, I’ve got papers to grade and my thesis is due next year and I’m literally dying. Professor Chase keeps bouncing it back for revisions. Dude won’t help me fix anything, just torches my drafts, then has the audacity to ask if I want to stick around for my PhD. Hard pass.\"","Eira smirked. \"So, no PhD with him then?\"","Lila obviously had zero idea. \"I’m hanging up on you now,\" she huffed, and did.","Eira laughed, got dressed, and called a car.","Kate texted saying they were close too. She waited curbside.","A Maybach glided up.","\"Alpha Killian, Eira’s here,\" Miles said, checking his phone.","Alpha Killian looked up. Blonde hair down past her shoulders, a white wool coat over dark jeans, gold hoops catching the streetlight. Simple, put-together, the kind of outfit that looked effortless but definitely wasn’t.","Second car pulled up right after. Kate and Natalie piled out, Natalie going straight for a hug, Kate right behind her.","Alpha Killian climbed out of his own car a beat later, dark suit, no tie, sleeves already looking like they wanted to be rolled up.","\"Alpha Killian,\" Eira said, tipping her chin up at him. He had a good six inches on her.","\"Hey.\" His eyes did a quick once-over, then he cleared his throat and looked away.","Everyone in, crew assembled.","Walking in together, the three of them looked like they’d coordinated it, Eira in white with that gold hair catching the restaurant lights, Kate in red, loud and unbothered, Natalie somewhere in between in something pastel and cute.","The guys next to them just had that boardroom energy, like they’d both walked straight out of a LinkedIn ad.","Heads turned as they cut through the restaurant.","A server clocked Alpha Killian instantly and rushed over. \"Right this way. Monica’s off tonight, but holler if you need anything.\""]},{"number":94,"title":"Chapter 94 Fresh Grounds","paragraphs":["Alpha Killian sat down first. Everyone else followed his lead.","Eira ended up between Alpha Killian on her left and Kate on her right.","The second she sat, she started passing out the gifts she’d hauled all the way here.","Alpha Killian first, since he was the boss. Everyone else got theirs at the same time, one in each hand.","Natalie clocked the packaging instantly. Her eyes went huge. \"Eira, can I open mine right now?\"","Nobody in this crew ever waited to open a gift.","Eira didn’t care either way. \"Go for it.\"","Green light given, everyone tore in.","\"The talking Baphomet plushie!\" Natalie clutched the blind box to her chest, practically buzzing. \"Thank you, Eira! Wait, here, this one’s yours!\" She shoved her own gift across the table.","Kate looked down at the row of sleek black lipstick tubes in front of her, eight of them, her exact shade family. Her mouth curved. \"These are perfect. Eira, this one’s mine.\"","\"And this is from me.\" Miles slid his gift over, all business. \"Thanks for the glasses chain.\"","Natalie grinned, evil. \"A glasses chain fits Miles so well. You know none of his glasses even have a prescription, right?\"","Eira blinked. Wait, what? Fake?","Miles pushed his glasses up with one finger, the ghost of a smile on his face. \"Glasses give off an invisible intelligence boost.\"","Eira almost lost it right there.","That left Alpha Killian’s gift, still sitting untouched. His was the only one that came in two parts.","Something a little too pleased flickered behind his eyes.","He opened the first box.","A bag of coffee beans, some small-batch roast.","Then the second.","A portable espresso maker, small enough to fit in a backpack.","Kate’s jaw dropped. \"Okay, hold on. Alpha Killian has been living off vending machine coffee for like three weeks straight and you just, what, fixed his entire personality?\"","Natalie slapped both hands over her mouth, grinning behind them. \"This might be the most thoughtful gift at this table and it’s not even close.\"","Miles muttered, just loud enough to catch, \"Yeah, nobody else stood a chance.\"","Eira felt her face heat up.","\"You’ve been running on maybe four hours of sleep,\" she said, aiming for casual. \"Figured the stuff from the break room was doing you dirty.\"","\"It has been.\" The corner of Alpha Killian’s mouth curved. He turned the espresso maker over in his hands, actually looking impressed. \"This beats anything I’ve bought for myself.\"","The table let out a round of oohs that Eira very much did not appreciate.","Alpha Killian let it die down on its own, clearly enjoying it a little too much.","Then he pulled out a gift box and set it in front of her. \"Open it.\"","She opened it right there. Inside sat a neat stack of bound documents.","She lifted them out.","Natalie, sitting across from her, couldn’t see the print, just blank white paper from the back.","\"Alpha Killian, who gives someone a stack of paperwork as a gift? What happened to normal presents?\" Natalie’s voice trailed off fast the second Alpha Killian’s stare cut toward her.","\"What Natalie means,\" Miles jumped in, save of the century, \"is that you two clearly think alike. Great minds.\"","Alpha Killian’s stare eased off Natalie, landed back on Eira, the amusement from a second ago settling into something quieter.","She hadn’t caught a word of that exchange. Her eyes were locked on the file.","Every payment Alpha Sebastian had made to Serena during the marriage, laid out in black and white.","Forget the three million a month in research funding, that was just the baseline.","In the month and a half since Serena got back stateside, the numbers ran into the hundreds of thousands, over and over again.","Alpha Sebastian really didn’t hold back. Not even close.","Four years married, and the biggest thing he’d ever spent on their life together was the down payment on their condo. That was it. That was the ceiling.","Guy would shortchange himself before he’d shortchange Serena.","Real romantic.","Eira’s fingers tightened slightly around the papers before she set them back in the box. She looked up, voice steady. \"Thank you, Alpha Killian. Really.\"","Alpha Killian’s easy mood from a minute ago was gone, something harder underneath it now. He took a sip of water. \"Just a fraction of it. Sterling’s reach doesn’t cover everything he’s got, but it’s enough.\" A beat. \"Keep it somewhere safe.\"","Leverage. As long as she had something on Alpha Sebastian, she’d never have to worry about him trying anything down the road.","Might come in handy someday.","\"Got it,\" Eira said.","--","Dinner started rolling out in waves, all of The Eden Garden’s signature dishes. A bottle of white wine showed up with the meal.","As the server moved to pour Eira’s glass, Alpha Killian’s voice cut in, casual on the surface. \"Light pour.\"","Everyone on his team could drink circles around a bar. Except Eira.","She wasn’t quite a one-glass lightweight, but two glasses in, she was done for the night. Alpha Killian had seen her drunk exactly once, glassy eyes, pink nose, looking like she’d shatter if anyone breathed on her wrong.","Once was enough. He wasn’t about to sit through that again.","Everyone raised their glasses.","Eira’s phone buzzed. She took a small sip of wine, then glanced down at the screen.","Beatrice: Oh my God, I just heard from Susan, your divorce is officially final. Congratulations, sweetheart.","Eira typed back fast, smiling at her phone. [Thank you, Beatrice. Couldn’t have done any of it without you and Susan.]","Alpha Killian caught the message out of the corner of his eye.","The divorce was final. Officially done.","The corner of his mouth curved, just barely, and he drained his glass in one smooth motion.","Eira set her phone down and pushed her chair back, rising to her feet. \"Quick toast.\" She lifted her glass. \"Thanks for having my back this past month, all of you. Seriously.\"","She took a small sip.","Then she turned to Alpha Killian. \"Alpha Killian, I owe you way more than a thank you—\"","\"Nah, you don’t.\" He looked up at her, something easy in his eyes. \"Just don’t forget it. That’s payment enough.\"","She blinked. \"Deal.\"","\"Good.\" He nodded once, took another sip.","He usually had an iron stomach when it came to alcohol. But something about tonight, the flush in her cheeks from the wine, the way she kept stealing small bites like she was pacing herself, had him feeling a little off his game anyway."]},{"number":95,"title":"Chapter 95 Static in the Air","paragraphs":["As dinner wound down, Kate and Natalie excused themselves to the restroom together.","Alpha Killian leaned back in his chair, one hand propped against his temple, eyes half-lidded, doing a pretty convincing impression of a guy who’d had way too much. His gaze slid over to Miles.","Miles caught the signal right away.","\"Eira,\" he said, smooth as ever, \"I think Alpha Killian might need a ride home. I’ll get Kate and Natalie back myself.\"","Out of everyone at the table, Eira had drunk the least. Her face was a little flushed, her head felt warm and pleasant, but she could still walk straight and talk just fine.","\"Alpha Killian, you drunk?\"","People who were actually drunk always swore up and down they weren’t.","\"Not drunk,\" Alpha Killian said, flat.","\"Yeah, that’s exactly what a drunk person says.\"","Miles kept his mouth shut, fighting a grin. Alpha Killian really committing to the bit.","\"His tolerance is honestly terrible,\" Eira added under her breath, shaking her head like she felt bad for him.","Alpha Killian said nothing, just let his head loll back against the seat for effect, playing it up.","Kate and Natalie came back from the restroom right then, still laughing about something between themselves.","Miles caught Kate’s eye, tilted his head toward the door, then turned to Eira. \"Hey, since he’s in no shape to get home on his own, and you’re headed that way anyway, mind taking him? I’ll drop these two off myself.\"","He scooped up Kate and Natalie’s bags and gifts before either of them could argue, ushering them toward the exit.","Alpha Killian stood up, movements a little loose, like he genuinely couldn’t be bothered to steady himself.","Eira rose too. \"Come on. Car’s out front, right? I’ll ride with you, make sure you actually get inside.\"","They walked out to the car together, Eira keeping a hand near his elbow just in case. The valet had it waiting at the curb already. She bent down to help him into the back seat, and the moment she let go of his arm, his hand shot out and caught her wrist.","She looked at him, confused. \"Alpha Killian?\"","His eyes lifted, just slightly, locked on her face, unreadable.","\"You’re divorced?\"","Eira froze. Did not see that question coming.","\"Caught it on your phone earlier,\" Alpha Killian said, plain as that.","\"Yesterday,\" Eira answered, just as plain. \"It’s final.\"","\"Congratulations.\" He said it flat, no real read on it either way, then let go of her wrist and nodded her toward the car.","The driver shut the door behind both of them, climbed back up front, and raised the privacy divider.","The back seat turned into its own little sealed-off world. Above them, the ceiling glowed with tiny pinpricks of fake starlight.","Eira looked up at it.","Alpha Killian followed her gaze. \"You into that?\"","\"Reminds me of the shelter roof,\" she said. \"Every full moon, all the pups used to sneak up there. Real stars, no city glow drowning them out.\" A small pause. \"Then the developers bought up half the block around us. Skyscrapers went up, lights never turned off. Couldn’t see a thing after that.\"","\"Sounds like a rough trade.\"","\"Yeah, well.\" She shrugged. \"Omegas don’t exactly get a say in zoning decisions.\"","Alpha Killian leaned back, one arm draped over the seat, looking about as relaxed as a guy who owned the whole city block. \"I’ve got a ranch. Private land, no lights for miles, wolves roam free out there most nights. Decent observatory deck too, if the view’s more your speed.\"","Eira glanced at him, waiting for the catch.","\"It’s mine,\" he said, before she could ask.","\"Of course it is,\" she muttered.","\"You good to drive, or are you still feeling it?\" She studied his face. Not even a hint of drunk left on him.","\"Mostly good.\"","\"So can I swing by your place tonight and grab my box? Rather not make it a whole separate trip.\"","Alpha Killian looked at her. Just the box, no other angle to it, no hidden ask. That was the thing about her, she never played games with him, not once, unlike every woman before her who’d tried some version of \"can I come up\" as a foot in the door.","Weirdly, that got under his skin more than it should have.","\"Just the box?\" Flat again.","\"What else would there be?\"","Alpha Killian went quiet for a second, eyes closed. Then he caught it, that faint floral warmth still clinging to her from dinner, the soft rustle of her shifting around next to him.","She was unwrapping something. One of the gifts from earlier.","He cracked one eye open. Eira was completely focused on the box in her lap, hadn’t noticed a thing.","Kate’s gift: silver filigree earrings, tiny pearls, catching the light. Natalie’s: ten hand creams, every scent under the sun. Miles’s: an engraved fountain pen, sleek black lacquer, easily the classiest gift of the bunch.","All solid gifts. Stuff she’d actually use.","Eira smiled to herself. She snapped a pic of the haul and posted it.","Caption: Shoutout to my coworkers, y’all didn’t have to but I appreciate it.","Replies came in hot.","Kate: wait is that a pen from Miles?? that man really said \"here’s some office supplies\" as his big romantic gesture","Miles: IT’S JUST A PEN. Kate I will not survive this","Natalie: Kate stop trying to get him fired","Natalie: jk. mostly.","Then Alpha Killian liked the post.","Alpha Killian was scrolling his own phone, jaw tight, mood gone somewhere dark.","Eira glanced up, confused.","\"You’re up,\"she said.","\"Mm.\"","Whatever had soured his mood, she couldn’t tell. She tucked the gifts back into her bag without asking.","The car rolled up to a gate marked Number Nine, Southridge Estates. Eira packed faster now, twisting her hair up and jabbing Miles’s pen through the bun to hold it in place, some old habit from all-nighters back in the lab, barely thinking about it.","Alpha Killian’s face darkened another notch.","\"Out,\" he said. Cold.","The car had already stopped in the circular driveway, a fountain going somewhere off to the side. Eira climbed out, feet barely on the pavement when a hand reached out and pulled the pen straight out of her hair.","It all came crashing down at once.","She spun around. Blonde hair fell across her face, half covering her eyes. Through the strands, she caught his stare.","Something flickered across his face for half a second before it smoothed back out.","She didn’t catch it.","She pushed her hair back. \"What’s your problem?\"","\"Looks better down.\" Alpha Killian pocketed the pen and headed for the house.","Eira stared after him. \"That’s my—\"","\"You coming or not? Thought you wanted your box.\"","She swallowed the word pen and jogged to catch up.","--","Silix Institute","Serena had just swiped her badge when a security guard stepped in front of her.","\"Dr. Winthrop, we need to run you through a routine check.\"","Serena stopped cold. \"Excuse me?\"","Nobody had ever pulled her aside for a check before. Not once.","\"Tight security this week. Orders from upstairs. We appreciate your cooperation, Dr. Winthrop.\"","Her face soured, but she kept quiet and walked through the body scanner anyway. They dumped her bag out on the side table, pulled out every device she had, and went through each one.","Did they honestly think this would stop her?","Cute."]},{"number":96,"title":"Chapter 96 Everything He Dried","paragraphs":["Inside, the grand foyer was packed with antique furniture, oil paintings, and glass cases full of ceramics that probably cost more than her whole yearly salary.","\"Would you care for some water, Miss Crawford?\" A middle-aged woman in a crisp apron came over with a tray, her face warm and welcoming. She gestured toward the sofa. \"Sit, make yourself at home.\"","Eira took the cup with a polite nod. \"You know who I am?\"","The woman blinked, then recovered fast. \"Miss Lila mentioned you. And, well, I might’ve caught a photo somewhere.\"","Luna Seraphina showed her, more like it.","\"You can call me Mrs. Jones,\" the woman added. \"Been looking after Alpha Killian for years now.\"","\"Mrs. Jones,\" Eira repeated.","Mrs. Jones lingered nearby, watching Eira with a look that could only be called doting. It was a little much, honestly, a little unsettling even.","\"Mrs. Jones.\" Alpha Killian’s voice cut through the moment sharp as a blade.","The housekeeper backed off, reluctant, clearly still cataloguing something about Eira in her head.","When Eira heard him coming down the stairs, she stood up fast.","He was carrying her box.","Her heart jumped. She rushed over, dropped down right there, and started pulling everything out piece by piece, laying it all across the floor.","The box itself looked rough, warped and wrinkled from water damage.","Panic flashed across her face. If the box looked this bad, what about everything inside it?","But when she unfolded one of her hand-bound sketchbooks, the pages came apart clean, no sticking. Some of the ink had bled a little, colors smudging at the edges, but the pages themselves held up fine.","She reached for one of the letters next. The envelope had already been opened.","The paper inside was dry. A little warped, but readable.","She looked up fast.","Alpha Killian met her eyes. \"I don’t make a habit of reading other people’s business.\"","Eira got it instantly. He’d dried everything out, piece by piece, by hand.","\"Thank you.\" Her eyes went a little glassy.","Alpha Killian thought, out of nowhere, that her eyes right then beat out anything he’d ever seen through a telescope.","\"You owe me.\"","\"I know, I know.\" Eira let out a small laugh, packing everything back into the box. She stood, looked him straight in the eye. \"Seriously though, Alpha Killian. Thank you. The hotel, Sebastian, now this. You’ve had my back more than I probably deserve.\"","Alpha Killian’s eye twitched.","\"Oh my gosh, so that’s Miss Crawford’s box!\" Mrs. Jones came flying back into the room, clapping her hands together like she’d just found out her favorite couple on Bridgerton finally got together.","\"Last time Alpha Killian brought it home, he spent the whole afternoon out on the balcony drying every single page. Wouldn’t let me touch a thing. Said he didn’t want anything ruined.\"","Luna Seraphina had been crystal clear about this: Killian’s great at annoying people and hiring good staff. Romance, though? Hopeless. If you ever meet Miss Crawford, help him out.","And Mrs. Jones fully intended to help.","She’d read every Colleen Hoover book on her shelf twice and rewatched Bridgerton more times than she’d admit out loud. She knew a slow burn when she saw one.","\"You know you’re the first woman he’s ever brought home, right? In all my years working here.\"","Alpha Killian’s jaw tightened. \"Mrs. Jones. That’s enough.\"","Eira blinked, thrown off completely. She’d spent most of her life in labs and lecture halls. Reading romantic subtext wasn’t exactly her specialty. And besides, her divorce had just gone final. Whatever this was supposed to be was the last thing on her radar right now.","\"Mrs. Jones, don’t you have something else to do?\" Alpha Killian’s voice had gone ice cold.","Mrs. Jones backed off, reluctant, already halfway to texting someone about this.","Eira turned to leave.","Her phone started buzzing, hard, over and over. Not a call. An alert. From the lab.","She pulled it out. The screen was lit up red, notifications stacking on top of each other.","She set the box down fast, on the coffee table this time instead of the floor, and looked up at Alpha Killian, urgency written all over her face.","\"Sorry, I gotta run. Can I leave this here for now? I’ll grab it later.\"","She didn’t even grab her bag.","Alpha Killian didn’t waste time arguing. The car that dropped them off had already left, so he got on the phone and called his guy to swing back around, fast.","Eira didn’t wait around either. She rattled off an address near the lab, then fired off a text to Professor Davies and Claire, her assistant.","Eira: someone got into my workstation. need you both there NOW","Professor Davies and Claire both scrambled to get there.","When the car pulled up to the address, Eira thanked the driver and hopped out. She ducked into a nearby alley, using it to slip out of sight.","The driver waited a second, then called Alpha Killian.","\"Alpha Killian, I dropped Miss Crawford off. Don’t think that was actually where she was headed, though.\"","\"Understood.\" Alpha Killian hung up. He didn’t push for more.","--","Eira had a pretty good idea who’d been snooping around her desk.","On her way to the lab, she swung by a corner store and grabbed a black mask, the kind that covers half your face, then pulled her hair forward to hide her profile. Straight-up disguise mode.","The guard at the gate nodded. \"Dr. Crawford.\"","\"Has Serena Winthrop been here tonight?\" Eira kept her voice low, sharp.","The guard nodded.","A few minutes later, Professor Davies’s car rolled up. He cracked the window and asked the exact same question.","The guard nodded again.","Professor Davies rolled the window back up, sat with it a second, jaw tight, like he hated what he was about to do.","He handed Claire his phone anyway. \"Text this to Dr. Victor Winthrop. Word for word, exactly what I say.\"","Claire hesitated. \"Wait, seriously? Shouldn’t we be reporting this straight to campus security, or the board? Why loop in her grandfather at all?\"","\"Because the second this hits the board, it’s already over.\" Professor Davies let out a tired, disgusted sigh. \"Winthrop’s name is on half the funding in this building. You really think anyone up top is gonna side with Eira over him? They’ll bury the report, and Eira’s the one who ends up looking like she caused a scene over nothing. This isn’t the smart move, Claire.\"","\"Oh.\" Claire looked down, finished typing, and handed the phone back, clearly not thrilled about it either. \"Sent.\"","They dropped their phones off at the entrance and headed for the lab building.","Sure enough, lights were on inside.","The two of them hurried in. Not a soul in sight, just the inner lab door hanging wide open.","Professor Davies and Claire stepped through. For a second, neither of them clocked who was actually sitting at the desk.","If it weren’t for the fact that her fingers were flying across the keyboard without tripping a single alarm, she could’ve passed for some rich kid who wandered in on a family connection.","\"What’s going on?\" Professor Davies came closer, eyes on the screen. Surveillance footage. Eira was pulling a copy onto a flash drive.","The grainy black-and-white clip showed Serena’s face, clear as day.","Professor Davies’s face dropped. Of course it was her.","\"Cameras in here got cut for a few minutes,\" Eira said, calm, steady. \"But I’ve got a mini cam wired into my own setup. Caught everything.\"","She reached to fire the footage straight off to the institute’s board.","Professor Davies grabbed her hand before she could hit send.","\"Not yet. Besides, she never actually got into the real data. Go after her now and you’ll hit walls everywhere you turn. Even if she gets bounced off this project, she lands on the next one, easy. She’s not going anywhere. Her grandfather makes sure of that. Her name stays spotless. Yours won’t. People will start ghosting you just to stay in his good graces.\"","Eira’s hand stayed locked on the mouse."]},{"number":97,"title":"Chapter 97 Damage Control","paragraphs":["Professor Davies’s voice dropped, gentler now. \"I know this hits you both ways, professionally and personally. But at least hold off until the project’s done. Somebody gets exposed now, the whole thing gets shut down. This was Dr. Thorne’s life’s work.\"","That last part got through to her. She let go.","Professor Davies closed the email window himself. \"Keep the footage. Don’t delete it.\" He paused. \"Did you run into her when you got here?\"","\"No. She must’ve felt something was off and bailed.\"","Eira stood and stepped back. Claire quietly pulled her out of the room.","When Dr. Victor Winthrop walked in, all three of them were standing there waiting.","\"I heard someone got into your lab data. Any idea who?\"","He wasn’t asking like someone trying to get to the bottom of things. He was asking like someone trying to get ahead of the story.","Eira lifted her gaze. \"Security here is airtight. Anyone within two kilometers with a phone camera gets stopped and questioned on the spot. Whoever got in and tripped that alarm came from inside this institute. There’s no other way it happens.\"","\"You didn’t see who it was?\" His tone turned stern. \"Was any data taken?\"","\"No,\" Eira said flatly.","He relaxed, just slightly. \"Then we’re fine.\"","If data had actually gotten out, this would’ve turned into a real problem. National security territory.","\"You’re not going to look into it, Dr. Winthrop?\" Eira kept her voice even.","He paused, then settled back into his usual tone, calm, sure of himself, the kind of voice that expected the conversation to end wherever he decided it would. \"An investigation would slow everything down. I’m guessing that’s not what you want either, Dr. Crawford.\"","Eira met his eyes without flinching.","That look threw him more than he expected.","\"That’s enough, then.\" He’d shown up for exactly one reason, to shut this down before it went any further.","\"Dr. Winthrop.\" Eira’s voice stayed quiet, sharp. \"I’d appreciate it if you kept your granddaughter in check.\"","He froze mid-step, turned back slow, his face going dark. \"Don’t throw around accusations you can’t back up.\"","\"It’s not hard to work out,\" Eira said. \"Every project runs its own lab. Leadership can get into any of them, but regular researchers only have access to whatever they’re assigned. I already checked. Everyone on my team has an alibi. Everyone except Serena.\"","He had nothing to say to that.","Professor Davies stayed quiet, playing dumb on purpose.","Claire had no real say in any of this, but her just standing there added weight to the room anyway.","Victor knew exactly what Eira could do to his granddaughter’s career if she wanted to go there. His face lost all its color.","He didn’t push back. \"This ends here.\" He left.","Claire finally let out the breath she’d been holding.","Professor Davies spoke quietly. \"He’ll deal with Serena. That much I know for sure.\"","--","Serena sat in her grandfather’s office, wound tight as a spring.","She’d worked so hard just to catch someone walking into the inner lab, one glance at the passcode, that’s all she needed. Memorize it, jot it down later, done.","Except they didn’t just lock the door. They wired the whole thing to an alarm.","So nobody gets to touch that data but Dr. Crawford? That’s not leadership, that’s hoarding. Why isn’t anyone calling this out?","The door swung open. Victor walked in.","Serena shot up. \"Grandfather.\"","For the first time since she’d gotten back from her program out in California, he actually raised his voice at her.","\"You have any clue what happens if Dr. Crawford reports you for trying to steal classified research? You’re done. I’m done. We’re talking federal espionage charges. Decades, easy.\"","She flinched. \"They don’t even know it was me. And I’m part of this project anyway, how’s that stealing? She’s the one sitting on everything.\"","\"You think the cops are dumb? Those cameras are just decoration? You cut the feed in your own lab and figured that made you invisible?\" Victor stared at her like he didn’t recognize his own granddaughter. \"So this is what you learned all those years overseas? Taking shortcuts instead of building real skills?\"","Her face went hot, anger and shame all tangled up. \"How can you talk to me like that? You’re the one who kept pushing me to publish! I rushed it because of Sebastian. I wanted to help him. I wanted us to make you proud.\"","\"I told you to sit on the publication.\" Victor’s voice sharpened. \"This is about the Hale kid, isn’t it?\"","Her eyes lit up. \"So you’ll actually help him? Back his company for the bid?\"","She stepped closer, hope all over her face.","Victor’s expression stayed hard, but Serena knew better. When he was really furious, he went dead quiet, ice cold. This was just noise.","\"You’d torch your own future over some guy. What else am I supposed to do?\" He sighed. \"Besides, I like the kid. Sharp. We’re picking the winner on merit this round, not connections.\"","\"Sorry, Grandfather. I shouldn’t have gone after the core data.\"","Even with the alarm blaring, she hadn’t panicked. She knew he’d bail her out. The only thing that had her nervous was how mad he’d be about it.","Victor was the one person on the planet Serena actually respected. And feared.","\"Dr. Crawford’s genuinely pissed this time,\" Victor said. \"Don’t pull this again. I can’t cover for you twice.\"","Serena pouted, stayed quiet a beat.","Victor exhaled. \"Alright, spit it out. What are you angling for?\"","\"Can I rep the project at the signing ceremony?\" Straight shot, no dancing around it.","\"No.\"","\"Why not?\"","\"Dr. Crawford’s the lead engineer. That spot’s hers. And even without her, it’d go to Professor Davies. Not you.\"","Her face dropped.","Victor studied her. \"You’ll get your turn. I’ll put you front and center, even if it means easing Professor Davies out. Guy’ll probably be relieved, honestly, hand the torch off, retire early, play golf, whatever old professors do with their free time.\"","\"Isn’t that kind of cold? He’s senior.\"","She wasn’t totally shameless about it. What actually bugged her was watching someone her own age outshine her at every turn, especially after getting frozen out of this project from day one.","But bigger than that, she’d already told Alpha Sebastian she was running point here. No way she could lose face in front of him now.","\"Cold how?\" Victor waved her off. \"Guy’s only got his title because he’s smooth and married into money. Take that away and he’s nobody. Someone like Dr. Thorne, who actually built something from scratch, that’s one in a million. Don’t lump the two together.\"","Something clicked behind Serena’s eyes. She smiled, sugar sweet. \"Got it. Thanks, Grandfather. No more trouble, I promise, scout’s honor.\"","\"Once this wraps, I’ll bump you up to something better. Eira won’t want you anywhere near her crew, but without this project backing her, she’s not exactly untouchable either.\"","Victor shot her one last look, warning written all over it. \"Stay in your lane. Stick to the plan. Your future’s solid if you don’t blow it.\"","\"Thank you, Grandfather.\" She looped her arm through his. \"Sebastian taught me how to make noodles from scratch. Let me cook for you tonight.\"","They walked out together, chatting easy.","And ran straight into Professor Davies, Claire, and Eira coming down the hall.","Face to face.","Serena’s eyes locked on the woman in the middle.","Finally.","Never got that photo last time. Now here she was, in the flesh.","Serena clocked her top to bottom. Tall. Sharp dressed. Put together.","But something felt off.","Why does she look so familiar?"]},{"number":98,"title":"Chapter 98 Growing Regret","paragraphs":["That silhouette. Serena ran through her mental files. She’d seen this woman somewhere before, she was sure of it.","The stare she leveled on Eira set off alarm bells for everyone watching, way too intense, way too unfriendly.","Professor Davies shot Claire a look. Claire got the memo instantly, stepped in front of Eira, blocked the view.","Eira ducked her gaze lower.","Sightline cut off, Serena moved to push forward. Victor grabbed her arm, hard.","\"What the hell are you thinking?\" His face went to stone. \"We’re leaving. Now.\" He dragged her off ahead of the others.","Professor Davies called after them. \"Take care, Dr. Winthrop.\"","Claire waited till they’d cleared the corridor, then let out a breath and slapped a hand to her chest. \"Okay, that scared the crap out of me. I thought she was gonna rip that mask right off and go full catfight on our lead engineer. The nerve on that girl.\"","\"You gotta understand who we’re dealing with.\" Professor Davies lowered his voice. \"Victor’s not just some department head. He sits on the executive board here at Silix. Half the funding in this building’s got his signature on it somewhere. Nobody on staff is gonna risk crossing him over his own granddaughter.\"","\"So that’s how she gets away with everything?\"","\"Pretty much. She’s been trailing him since she was a kid, sitting in on board meetings, meeting people most researchers never get within ten feet of. Picked up plenty of bad habits along the way too, talked back to senior staff, pulled rank she didn’t actually have. Nobody ever called her out on it. Why would they? Cross her, and you’re crossing him.\"","Professor Davies watched the two of them disappear down the hall, then shook his head and turned to Eira. \"You good?\"","Eira shook her head. \"I’m fine.\"","She wasn’t, though. Not really. Something told her Serena might’ve already put two and two together about who she was.","Professor Davies caught the look on her face before she said a word. \"We’re only a few days out from wrapping this. Even if she puts it together, her hands are tied. Victor’s got too much riding on this project himself, funding, reputation, his own standing on the board. I’ll have a word with him. He’ll keep her on a short leash, guaranteed.\"","Eira nodded. \"Thanks, Professor.\"","The three of them started walking.","Professor Davies asked, \"So, how have you been? You’re officially off the books at Sterling Group now?\"","\"Yeah, it’s been great. Was actually at a going-away dinner when the alarm went off, came straight here.\" Eira glanced at Claire. No point hiding it anymore. \"Sebastian and I are officially divorced. Papers came through today.\"","Professor Davies just nodded, no reaction.","Claire stopped dead. \"Hold up, you’re divorced? Like, for real, done, signed and everything?\"","She’d known Eira was married since day one on this job. Knew she took that marriage seriously too, every time she brought her husband up, something in her face went soft. Cooking, cleaning, none of it ever fazed her.","Three years watching this woman run herself into the ground, juggling work and home like some kind of machine.","And now, out of nowhere, single.","Claire skipped the questions and just went in for the hug, arms locked around her so tight it was basically a tackle. Eira’s arms stayed pinned, no wiggle room at all.","\"You don’t gotta kill yourself for anyone anymore,\" Claire said, voice wobbling, right on the edge of tears.","Eira let out a strained laugh. \"Okay, you’re crushing my ribs here.\"","\"Oh, my bad.\" Claire let go fast.","They reached the entrance just in time to catch Victor shoving Serena into the car.","Serena shot one last look back at Eira as she climbed in.","\"Eyes front. You hear me?\" Victor was done, tapped out, zero patience left for his granddaughter. He was hauling her home and putting her on house arrest, no debate.","Serena tried to explain. \"I just wanted to see what she actually looks like. She’s always covering herself up. Is she hideous under there or something?\"","\"Ugly or not, it’s none of your business.\"","The car door slammed shut.","Victor glared at her. \"Don’t you dare pull a stunt like that again. Next time, I won’t be able to cover for you. You are not taking my name down with you.\"","\"Grandfather!\" Serena looked genuinely hurt now, and angry. \"So I’m an embarrassment to you? Is that what you’re saying?\"","Victor kept his eyes on the road, face cold. He didn’t say a word.","That only made her angrier.","How could he think that about her?","Back at the Winthrop estate, Serena didn’t even stop to take her shoes off. She stormed straight upstairs and slammed her bedroom door hard enough to rattle the walls.","The staff exchanged looks. They’d seen this movie before, grandfather and granddaughter locking horns.","Out of the entire Winthrop family, Serena was the only one who ever dared throw a fit in front of the old man. He’d raised her that way himself, and no matter how worked up he got, he never stayed mad for long.","Victor turned to the staff. \"Keep an eye on Serena this week. She doesn’t leave the house.\"","One of them blinked. House arrest?","\"Watch her close,\" Victor said again.","This time, he meant it.","--","Upstairs, Serena, fresh off getting grounded, slammed her door again and grabbed her phone. Called Alpha Sebastian.","Third try before he picked up.","\"What took you so long?\"","\"Still at the office.\"","\"This late?\" Surprise, then her tone melted. \"Why’re you still grinding? Thought everything was locked in already.\"","\"Running through it one more time. Can’t afford to screw this bid up.\"","\"This is on me, Sebastian. Couldn’t do more to back you up. Grandfather already chewed me out over it, got me stuck at home, can’t even step outside.\"","His brow creased. \"Serena, you really shouldn’t have told me that much. Could’ve blown up in your face.\"","\"So now you’re blaming me too?\" Tone snapping, anger bleeding through. \"I did it for you.\"","\"I’m just worried you’re gonna get burned over this. That’s it.\" He sighed. \"Gotta get back to it. We’ll catch up once this whole thing’s done.\"","He hung up, tossed the phone aside, pinched the bridge of his nose. Head back, running on fumes.","The bid wasn’t the only thing keeping him up. He was also racing to lock down Dr. Shaw’s patent, needed it wrapped before year end so his numbers looked good walking into the big annual meeting at Carter Group.","He reached for his glass of water. Stone-cold.","His assistant and secretary had both left hours ago. The entire office was silent.","He was alone.","If I were home right now...","Eira would’ve clocked how wrecked he looked in about two seconds. Would’ve handed him something hot to drink, dug out the neck massager before he even asked.","Then it hit him: last month, when he’d barely made it home some nights, she’d told him he was running himself into the ground and made him haul the massager to the office with him. He dug through his desk drawers, found it at the very bottom, still in the box, never opened. A gift from Eira.","He sat there holding it, and for the first time in weeks, he actually missed her.","He fired off a text.","[You up?]","Nothing.","Texted his assistant instead.","[Car locked in yet? Once it’s bought, get her signed up for driving lessons too. Don’t want her onto it early.]","Assistant sent back a few picks. All twenty to thirty grand, nothing fancy.","Alpha Sebastian called him straight up. \"Why didn’t you go bigger?\"","Beat of silence. Then, careful: \"Alpha... didn’t you say Luna Eira wouldn’t want anything too flashy?\""]},{"number":99,"title":"Chapter 99 Apology and Revenge","paragraphs":["Alpha Sebastian was about to swear up and down he’d never said anything like that, when it hit him.","Last year. Rainy night. Eira walking home, umbrella in one hand, grocery bags in the other, rain running straight down the side of the umbrella and soaking her free hand clean through.","He’d actually thought about getting her a car back then. His assistant pulled up options fast, some pushing eighty, ninety grand, a couple hitting six figures.","And yeah. He’d said it. She doesn’t need anything that fancy.","He meant to buy one anyway.","Then that same week he’d had to push a big chunk of funding over to Serena’s research, and once that was locked in, he figured the car could wait a few more days.","A few more days turned into never.","Later on, when he asked Eira if she wanted a car, she said no, and he just let it drop, didn’t think twice.","Alpha Sebastian snapped back to the present. \"Get her a Porsche.\"","\"You got it, Alpha.\"","He hung up and started toward the door, intending to go home. Then he remembered—Eira wasn’t there.","He stopped cold, halfway across the room.","Eventually he just turned around and crashed on the couch in the private lounge off his office instead.","--","The next morning, Isabella blew up his phone until he woke up.","He grabbed it, squinted. Eight a.m.","\"Why are you blowing up my phone this early?\" he grumbled.","\"Sebastian, I’m freaking out.\" Isabella’s voice shook. \"Eira texted me. Wants to meet tonight. Ten p.m. The Sterling House.\"","\"So show up, say sorry, and move on. It’s not that deep. But you’ve gotta actually stop pulling stunts that mess with her, Isabella. I mean it this time.\"","\"You’re not listening to me!\" Her voice spiked, sharp enough to make him wince. \"Same time, same spot as last time. This has setup written all over it.\"","The screech rang straight through his skull. He pulled the phone back, got up, walked out of the lounge.","\"She’s not gonna do anything to you.\"","\"You don’t know that. Just come with me, okay? I need backup on this.\"","\"I don’t have time for this.\"","Even as the words left his mouth, though, something nagged at him. He hadn’t actually seen Eira in days. He exhaled.","\"Fine. I’ll swing by. But you’re going in first, I’m not babysitting this.\"","\"Knew you’d cave.\" Isabella’s tone flipped instantly, smug now instead of scared.","--","The Sterling House","Eira and Lila were already at the table when Isabella walked in.","Fruit, sparkling water, nobody touching either. Just waiting.","Lila dug through her bag as the clock ticked toward ten.","\"Brought something good.\" She pulled out a bottle of Vitamin C tablets, popped the cap. \"Watch. I drop one in her drink right in front of her, she’s gonna flip out.\"","She popped one in her own mouth. \"Ugh, sour as hell. No wonder people buy the fizzy kind.\"","Eira took one too, then reached for the bottle as Lila peeled at the label.","\"Leave it on,\" Eira said. \"Scarier that way.\"","Guilty people always figure everyone else is guilty too.","\"There she is.\" Lila smirked. \"Already looks paranoid.\"","Eira left the bottle out in plain sight and watched Isabella walk over.","Isabella dropped into her seat, already on the defensive. \"My brother’s on his way. Try anything, Eira, and he’ll cut you loose so fast.\"","Lila snorted. [Cut loose? Girl, he already did. Past tense.]","If Eira hadn’t promised his parents she’d keep the divorce quiet, Lila would’ve had it on every billboard downtown by now.","\"What’s funny?\" Isabella snapped at Lila, then turned back to Eira. \"You want an apology, fine, I’m here. Why’s there an audience?\"","\"So you can’t turn around tomorrow and say this never happened.\" Eira’s voice stayed flat. \"That’s the whole point of witnesses.\"","Isabella had nothing.","Lila leaned in. \"So? Let’s hear it.\"","\"Here?\" Isabella glanced around the room, looking sick to her stomach.","Lila pulled a megaphone out from under the table, dropped it with a thud. \"Here. On record, in front of people who’ll remember it.\"","\"Where’d that even come from?\" Eira blinked.","\"Under the table this whole time.\"","Lila slid it across. \"Say what you did, ask forgiveness, done. Short and sweet.\"","Isabella stared at it like it was radioactive. \"You can’t do this trashy stunt in a place like this.\"","\"My family owns it.\" Lila shrugged. \"Nobody’s saying a word.\"","Isabella’s jaw clenched hard enough to crack a molar. \"You’re doing this on purpose.\"","\"Yep.\" Eira glanced at her watch. \"Sixty seconds. Talk, or the deal’s off.\"","Isabella’s hands shook picking up the megaphone. She couldn’t do it, not in front of a room full of strangers.","Eira stood. Lila stood.","\"I’M SORRY!\" Isabella screamed into it, eyes squeezed shut. Every head turned. Her face went white.","\"I’m sorry, I shouldn’t have, I hated you, I wanted him to divorce you, I put something in your drink, I had someone, whatever, I’m sorry, forgive me!\"","She said it all in one breath, then buried her face in her hands.","Lila laughed. No mercy at all.","Eira sat back down, calm as ever. \"Now drink this.\"","\"What?\" Isabella’s head snapped up.","Eira twisted the cap, tapped two pills into a glass of wine, slid it over.","\"What are you doing?!\"","\"Drink it. Consider it Exhibit A.\"","\"I knew it!\" Isabella smacked the glass off the table. Glass everywhere.","Lila raised a hand. A server appeared instantly.","\"Fresh glass, please.\"","He brought one.","Lila poured, Eira dropped in two more pills, pushed it forward again.","Isabella whipped out her phone instead of grabbing anyone. \"I’m calling the cops right now. She’s drugging drinks in public, are you kidding me?\"","Nobody missed the irony, her throwing Eira’s own accusation right back at her, word for word.","\"Oh, now you’re worried about drugged drinks.\" Lila’s laugh went cold. \"Relax. It’s vitamin C. Read the label.\"","\"It really is just vitamin C,\" Eira added.","\"BULLSHIT!\" Isabella screeched, thumb still hovering over the call button, when she spotted someone behind Eira and forgot the phone entirely.","\"Sebastian!\" She lunged, grabbed his arm. \"She put something in the wine! She’s trying to force me to drink it!\"","His eyes dropped to the table. Pills still sitting there, undissolved, plain as day.","\"Eira?\"","Her eyes cut to him, cool and unbothered. She stood, glass in hand, stepped right in front of him.","\"Isabella.\" Soft voice. \"You want to know what forcing someone to drink actually looks like?\"","Her hand shot out, grabbed Isabella’s jaw, tipped her head back. Glass to her lips.","She tilted it. Wine poured straight in. Isabella’s eyes bulged, she sputtered, choked, flailed.","\"This is forcing someone to drink.\""]},{"number":100,"title":"Chapter 100 the dissolution certificate Left Behind","paragraphs":["Wine spilled down Isabella’s chin, soaked into her blouse. Teeth clamped shut, face twisted in pain.","\"Enough.\" Alpha Sebastian’s hand locked around Eira’s wrist. \"Eira. Enough.\"","Lila crossed her arms. \"Alpha Sebastian, she chokes down a few ounces of wine and you’re already losing it? Where were you when someone was forcing stuff on Eira?\"","Alpha Sebastian froze.","He hadn’t seen the state Eira was in that night.","But he’d seen what came after, water flooding the hallway. Seen her later at Dr. Wood’s clinic, drained white, hollowed out.","His grip loosened.","Lila leaned in, voice sharper. \"So your family only picks on her ’cause she’s got nobody? News flash, times changed. She’s got me now.\"","She snatched the glass back, pressed it to Isabella’s mouth, tipped it without mercy. Last of the wine went down. Set the empty glass down, hard clink.","Eira let go of her jaw.","Isabella crumpled, coughing hard, trying to force it back up. Nothing came. Panic set in.","\"Sebastian, call 911! Call someone!\"","He dropped down, arms around her. \"There’s nothing in it. It’s wine. You’re fine.\"","\"There is something in it, I know it!\"","Lila laughed, cold.","Eira dialed her lawyer, didn’t even look away from the two of them. Spoke clear, loud enough for both to hear. \"Yeah. Dropping the charges.\"","Hung up. Looked down at Isabella.","\"Last warning. Got your whole confession on tape tonight, motive and all. Come near me again, and nothing’s getting dropped next time.\"","Isabella’s eyes went wide. \"You recorded me? You sneaky-\"","Eira was already turning to Lila. \"We’re done here.\"","Lila grabbed her bag, crouched, set the megaphone and the vitamin bottle right in front of Isabella’s tear-streaked face.","\"Keep ’em. Souvenirs.\"","Isabella grabbed a pill, bit down. Sour. Just vitamin C.","She burst into tears from the relief alone.","Alpha Sebastian pulled his sister up, turned to follow Eira. Isabella grabbed his arm with both hands.","\"Sebastian, my legs, I can’t-\"","\"You’re fine. Go home.\"","He shook her off and headed for the elevators.","--","Eira and Lila were already inside the elevator when he rounded the corner. Eira’s finger hovered over the first-floor button. Then she spotted him.","\"Close it,\" she muttered.","\"Trying.\" Lila’s thumb was already hammering the button like her life depended on it.","Alpha Sebastian broke into a jog. Two steps away-","Doors slid shut.","Both women let out a breath.","\"Thank God,\" Eira whispered.","\"Clingy as hell,\" Lila muttered back.","Eira’s phone buzzed. Text from Alpha Sebastian: Wait for me downstairs.","She reached over, hit four random floor buttons instead.","\"Pick one,\" she said.","Lila grinned. \"Sixty-six. I’ve got a suite up there. You’re crashing with me tonight. Weekend anyway, and you already quit your job, right?\"","They got off on sixty-six.","Alpha Sebastian, meanwhile, took the other elevator straight down to the lobby. No sign of them. Rushed outside. Still nothing.","He called her.","No answer.","Half an hour later, a text finally came through: Phone died.","By then he was already driving Isabella home. Called again immediately.","\"Why didn’t you wait downstairs?\"","\"Didn’t want to see Isabella.\"","The bluntness threw him for a second. The old Eira never talked like that, so direct, no cushion. She used to soften everything, even when it came to his family.","From the passenger seat, Isabella’s voice shot up. \"Oh, like I wanted to see her, that manipulative little-\"","Alpha Sebastian hung up.","He’d been trying to smooth things over. Instead, the gap between them just kept widening.","A guy who could handle boardrooms and corporate politics without breaking a sweat, and he couldn’t manage his own family to save his life.","Alpha Sebastian rubbed his face, wiped out. Then slammed his palm against the steering wheel.","\"Isabella. You want me to divorce her? Is that what this is?\"","Isabella flinched. \"Whose side are you even on?\"","\"Whose side are you on?!\"","\"Dad’s! Mom’s! Serena’s! I’m on our family’s side!\" Isabella crossed her arms. \"None of us like Eira, that’s not our problem, that’s hers. If she was worth liking, we’d like her. Everybody loves Serena. Why? Because Serena’s just better.\"","Alpha Sebastian slammed the brakes. \"Get out.\"","\"No.\"","\"Get. Out.\"","\"You leave me on the side of the road, I’m calling Mom and Dad right now.\"","\"I said get out.\"","He needed to find Eira. Didn’t have time for this.","Isabella grabbed the handle above her seat. \"You are not leaving me here! I’m calling them right now!\"","\"Hey Siri. Call Dad.\"","The call connected instantly.","\"Dad! Mom! Help! Sebastian’s kicking me out of the car! He’s picking Eira over his own sister and he’s about to dump me on the street!\"","Alpha Sebastian’s head throbbed.","Their father’s voice boomed through the speaker. \"You’d actually leave your sister stranded on the side of the road?\"","Their mother jumped in next, voice shrill, dripping drama. \"If anything happens to Isabella, I swear I won’t survive it, Sebastian! You hear me?!\"","Isabella sniffled loud enough for the phone to pick it up. \"He hates me. He actually hates me.\"","\"Enough.\" Alpha Sebastian shot her a look, cold, sharp, completely out of patience.","Isabella’s breath caught. She hung up fast and went dead quiet.","Alpha Sebastian started the car again, drove her home without another word.","The silence was worse than any yelling. Isabella kept texting their parents under the seat, shooting nervous glances at her brother the whole ride. He caught every single one. Said nothing.","When they pulled up to the house, their parents were already waiting in the foyer.","Their mother lit up. \"Sebastian! You’re home!\"","Like the phone call five minutes ago never happened.","\"Just grabbing something from the study. Then I’m out.\"","He walked straight past both of them.","The second the study door swung open, their mother shot up out of her seat.","\"Wait-!\"","Too late.","The Mate Bond Dissolution certificate was sitting right there on the desk, along with both his Registered Mate Bond certificate.","She’d figured keeping that stuff lying around was bad luck, meant to toss it out days ago, and then completely forgot.","Now Alpha Sebastian was two seconds away from seeing all of it."]}]);
